window.I11_DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit":1,"theme":"Crops & Farming 作物與耕作","cards":[{"w":"arable","p":"adj.","d":"suitable for growing crops","c":"可耕種的","s":"Only a small part of Taiwan's land is arable because most of the island is covered by mountains, so farmers must use every flat field carefully.","t":"台灣只有一小部分土地是可耕種的，因為島上大部分被山脈覆蓋，所以農民必須小心利用每一塊平地。"},{"w":"wheat","p":"n.","d":"a grain plant used to make flour and bread","c":"小麥","s":"Most of the bread we eat is made from wheat, but Taiwan imports almost all of it because the climate is too wet to grow it well.","t":"我們吃的大部分麵包是用小麥做的，但台灣幾乎全部仰賴進口，因為氣候太潮濕而不容易種植。"},{"w":"rice paddy","p":"n.","d":"a flooded field where rice is grown","c":"稻田","s":"When we took the train through Yilan in spring, every rice paddy shone like a mirror, and my little brother kept taking photos of them.","t":"春天我們搭火車經過宜蘭時，每一片稻田都像鏡子一樣閃閃發亮，我弟弟一直不停地拍照。"},{"w":"maize","p":"n.","d":"a tall plant with yellow seeds; corn","c":"玉米","s":"Much of the maize grown in the United States is fed to animals, while only a small amount is eaten directly by people.","t":"美國種植的大部分玉米被拿來餵動物，而只有一小部分是直接供人食用。"},{"w":"barley","p":"n.","d":"a grain used for food, animal feed and making drinks","c":"大麥","s":"My grandmother often makes a warm barley tea in winter because she believes it is good for digestion, and the whole kitchen smells wonderful.","t":"我奶奶冬天常煮熱熱的大麥茶，因為她相信這對消化有好處，而且整個廚房都很香。"},{"w":"soybean","p":"n.","d":"a bean used to make tofu, soy milk and oil","c":"黃豆；大豆","s":"Tofu and soy milk both come from the soybean, so it is an important source of protein for many vegetarians in Asia.","t":"豆腐和豆漿都來自黃豆，所以它是亞洲許多素食者重要的蛋白質來源。"},{"w":"cash crop","p":"n.","d":"a crop grown to sell rather than to eat at home","c":"經濟作物","s":"Coffee is a popular cash crop in the mountains of Yunlin, and many young farmers have returned home because it brings a good income.","t":"咖啡是雲林山區很受歡迎的經濟作物，而且許多年輕農民因為它能帶來不錯的收入而返鄉。"},{"w":"crop rotation","p":"n.","d":"growing different crops in a field in different years","c":"輪作","s":"The farmer uses crop rotation every year, so he plants beans after corn because the beans put goodness back into the soil.","t":"這位農夫每年都採用輪作，所以他在玉米之後種豆類，因為豆類能讓土壤恢復養分。"},{"w":"monoculture","p":"n.","d":"growing only one type of crop over a large area","c":"單一作物栽培","s":"Huge areas of monoculture look neat from the air, but one disease can destroy the whole farm because every plant is the same.","t":"大面積的單一作物栽培從空中看起來很整齊，但一種病害就能摧毀整片農場，因為每株植物都一樣。"},{"w":"orchard","p":"n.","d":"a piece of land where fruit trees are grown","c":"果園","s":"We visited a strawberry farm and an apple orchard in Taichung, and the owner let us pick and eat fruit straight from the trees.","t":"我們參觀了台中的草莓園和蘋果果園，而且園主讓我們直接從樹上摘水果來吃。"},{"w":"vineyard","p":"n.","d":"a farm where grapes are grown","c":"葡萄園","s":"The family has run the vineyard for three generations, and they still pick the grapes by hand because machines might damage them.","t":"這個家族經營這座葡萄園已經三代了，而且他們仍然用手摘葡萄，因為機器可能會損傷葡萄。"},{"w":"greenhouse","p":"n.","d":"a glass building where plants are grown in warm conditions","c":"溫室","s":"Tomatoes grow well in the greenhouse even in winter, because the glass keeps the heat in and protects the plants from heavy rain.","t":"即使在冬天，番茄在溫室裡也長得很好，因為玻璃能保住熱度並保護植物不受大雨侵襲。"},{"w":"seedling","p":"n.","d":"a very young plant grown from a seed","c":"幼苗","s":"We planted each seedling in a small pot on the balcony, and after three weeks they were strong enough to move into the garden.","t":"我們把每一株幼苗種在陽台的小盆子裡，三個星期後它們就長得夠壯，可以移植到花園了。"},{"w":"germinate","p":"v.","d":"(of a seed) to start to grow","c":"發芽","s":"The beans will germinate in about five days if you keep the cotton wet, but they will fail if the room is too cold.","t":"如果你讓棉花保持濕潤，豆子大約五天就會發芽，但如果房間太冷，它們就長不出來。"},{"w":"ripen","p":"v.","d":"to become ready to eat","c":"成熟","s":"Bananas ripen faster in a paper bag, so my mother puts the green ones in a bag and waits a couple of days.","t":"香蕉放在紙袋裡會更快成熟，所以我媽媽把綠色的香蕉放進袋子裡，再等個兩三天。"},{"w":"weed","p":"n.","d":"a wild plant growing where it is not wanted","c":"雜草","s":"Every Saturday my grandfather pulls out the weed in his vegetable garden, because they steal water and sunlight from his cabbages.","t":"每個星期六我爺爺都會拔掉菜園裡的雜草，因為它們會搶走高麗菜的水分和陽光。"},{"w":"insecticide","p":"n.","d":"a chemical used to kill insects","c":"殺蟲劑","s":"The farmer stopped spraying insecticide on his fruit trees, and he now uses natural methods because he wants to protect the bees.","t":"這位農夫不再對果樹噴灑殺蟲劑，現在改用天然的方法，因為他想保護蜜蜂。"},{"w":"herbicide","p":"n.","d":"a chemical used to kill unwanted plants","c":"除草劑","s":"Some farmers spray herbicide to kill weeds quickly, but scientists worry that the chemicals can enter rivers and harm fish.","t":"有些農民噴灑除草劑來快速除草，但科學家擔心這些化學物質會流入河川並傷害魚類。"},{"w":"pollination","p":"n.","d":"moving pollen between flowers so that fruit can grow","c":"授粉","s":"Bees are essential for the pollination of many fruit trees, so farmers often rent hives when their orchards are in flower.","t":"蜜蜂對許多果樹的授粉至關重要，所以農民常在果園開花時租用蜂箱。"},{"w":"bumper crop","p":"n.","d":"an unusually large harvest","c":"大豐收","s":"The weather was perfect this year, and the farmers enjoyed a bumper crop of mangoes, but prices fell because there was so much fruit.","t":"今年天氣非常好，農民的芒果迎來大豐收，但因為水果太多，價格反而下跌了。"},{"w":"plantation","p":"n.","d":"a large farm growing one crop such as tea or rubber","c":"大型農園；種植園","s":"We visited a tea plantation in Nantou, and the workers showed us how they pick only the youngest leaves by hand.","t":"我們參觀了南投的一座茶葉種植園，而且工人示範他們如何只用手摘下最嫩的葉子。"},{"w":"smallholder","p":"n.","d":"a farmer who owns or rents a small piece of land","c":"小農","s":"Most rice in Taiwan is grown by a smallholder with only a few fields, so these farmers often work together to buy machines.","t":"台灣大部分的稻米是由只有幾塊田的小農種植的，所以這些農民常合作購買機器。"},{"w":"agronomist","p":"n.","d":"a scientist who studies soil and crops","c":"農藝學家","s":"An agronomist visited the village to test the soil, and she advised the farmers to plant beans because the land lacked nitrogen.","t":"一位農藝學家來到村裡檢測土壤，她建議農民種豆類，因為土地缺乏氮。"},{"w":"horticulture","p":"n.","d":"the study and practice of growing fruit, vegetables and flowers","c":"園藝學","s":"My cousin is studying horticulture at university, and she hopes to open a flower farm because she loves working with plants.","t":"我表姊在大學攻讀園藝學，她希望開一間花卉農場，因為她很喜歡和植物一起工作。"},{"w":"fallow","p":"adj.","d":"(of land) left without crops for a period to recover","c":"休耕的","s":"The farmer leaves one field fallow every few years, because the soil needs time to rest and recover its strength.","t":"這位農夫每隔幾年就讓一塊田休耕，因為土壤需要時間休息並恢復地力。"},{"w":"till","p":"v.","d":"to prepare and turn over soil for growing crops","c":"耕（地）","s":"In the past, farmers used water buffalo to till the fields, but today most of them use small machines because they are faster.","t":"過去農民用水牛來耕田，但現在大多數人使用小型機器，因為速度比較快。"},{"w":"sugar cane","p":"n.","d":"a tall plant whose stems are used to make sugar","c":"甘蔗","s":"Southern Taiwan once had many fields of sugar cane, and old sugar factories in Kaohsiung and Tainan have now become popular museums.","t":"南台灣過去有許多甘蔗田，而高雄和台南的老糖廠如今已成為熱門的博物館。"},{"w":"scarecrow","p":"n.","d":"a figure dressed in old clothes to frighten birds away from crops","c":"稻草人","s":"The children made a funny scarecrow for the school garden, but the clever birds soon realised it was not a real person.","t":"孩子們為學校菜園做了一個好笑的稻草人，但聰明的鳥兒很快就發現它不是真人。"},{"w":"reap","p":"v.","d":"to cut and collect a crop","c":"收割","s":"The villagers work together to reap the rice in autumn, and afterwards they share a big meal to celebrate the end of the season.","t":"村民在秋天一起收割稻子，之後他們會共享一頓大餐來慶祝這一季的結束。"}]},{"unit":2,"theme":"Soil, Water & Farm Equipment 土壤、水與農具","cards":[{"w":"soil","p":"n.","d":"the top layer of earth in which plants grow","c":"土壤","s":"Healthy soil is full of tiny living things, and it can hold water much better than dry dust after a long drought.","t":"健康的土壤充滿微小的生物，而且在長期乾旱後，它比乾燥的塵土更能保住水分。"},{"w":"nutrient","p":"n.","d":"a substance that helps plants, animals or people grow","c":"養分；營養素","s":"Plants take in each nutrient they need through their roots, so farmers test the soil to see what is missing.","t":"植物透過根部吸收所需的每一種養分，所以農民會檢測土壤，看看缺少了什麼。"},{"w":"nitrogen","p":"n.","d":"a gas that plants need to grow green leaves","c":"氮","s":"Beans can add nitrogen to the soil, so organic farmers plant them between other crops instead of buying chemical fertilisers.","t":"豆類能為土壤增加氮，所以有機農民把它們種在其他作物之間，而不是購買化學肥料。"},{"w":"manure","p":"n.","d":"animal waste put on land to help crops grow","c":"糞肥","s":"The farm smelled terrible after the workers spread manure on the fields, but the vegetables grew very well later that year.","t":"工人在田裡撒了糞肥之後農場臭氣沖天，但那年稍晚蔬菜長得非常好。"},{"w":"mulch","p":"n.","d":"material like leaves or straw spread over soil to keep it moist","c":"覆蓋物（護根）","s":"We put a thick layer of mulch around the young trees, so the soil stays damp and weeds cannot grow easily.","t":"我們在小樹周圍鋪了一層厚厚的覆蓋物，所以土壤能保持濕潤，雜草也不容易生長。"},{"w":"soil degradation","p":"n.","d":"the loss of soil quality and health","c":"土壤劣化","s":"Too many chemicals and heavy machines can cause soil degradation, and farmers then need even more fertiliser to grow the same amount of food.","t":"過多的化學物質和重型機具會造成土壤劣化，於是農民需要更多肥料才能種出同樣多的糧食。"},{"w":"salinisation","p":"n.","d":"the process of soil becoming too salty","c":"鹽化","s":"Near the coast, seawater has caused the salinisation of many fields, so rice no longer grows there and some farmers have left.","t":"在沿海地區，海水造成許多農田鹽化，所以那裡不再能種稻，有些農民也已經離開。"},{"w":"sprinkler","p":"n.","d":"a device that sprays water over plants or grass","c":"灑水器","s":"The sprinkler turns on automatically at six every morning, so the vegetables get water before the sun becomes too hot.","t":"灑水器每天早上六點會自動開啟，所以蔬菜能在太陽變得太熱之前得到水分。"},{"w":"drip irrigation","p":"n.","d":"watering plants slowly through small tubes near their roots","c":"滴灌","s":"Farmers in dry areas often use drip irrigation because it sends water straight to the roots, and very little is lost to the sun.","t":"乾燥地區的農民常使用滴灌，因為它把水直接送到根部，而且很少因日曬而流失。"},{"w":"groundwater","p":"n.","d":"water held under the ground in soil or rocks","c":"地下水","s":"Some fish farmers pump too much groundwater, and as a result the land in parts of Pingtung has slowly sunk.","t":"有些養殖業者抽取過多地下水，結果屏東部分地區的地面慢慢下陷了。"},{"w":"aquifer","p":"n.","d":"a layer of rock under the ground that holds water","c":"含水層","s":"The town gets its drinking water from a deep aquifer, but scientists warn that it will run dry if farms keep using so much.","t":"這個小鎮的飲用水來自一個很深的含水層，但科學家警告，如果農場繼續大量用水，它就會枯竭。"},{"w":"water table","p":"n.","d":"the level below which the ground is full of water","c":"地下水位","s":"The water table has dropped by several metres in recent years, so farmers must dig deeper wells to reach water.","t":"近年來地下水位已下降了好幾公尺，所以農民必須挖更深的井才能取到水。"},{"w":"tractor","p":"n.","d":"a strong farm vehicle used to pull machines","c":"拖拉機；耕耘機","s":"My uncle drives a small tractor to prepare his fields, and he lets the children ride on it when they visit the farm.","t":"我叔叔開一台小型耕耘機來整地，而且孩子們到農場玩時他會讓他們坐上去。"},{"w":"combine harvester","p":"n.","d":"a large machine that cuts and cleans grain in one go","c":"聯合收割機","s":"A single combine harvester can do the work of dozens of people, so a rice field that once took a week is now finished in an afternoon.","t":"一台聯合收割機能完成好幾十個人的工作，所以以前要花一週的稻田，現在一個下午就收割完了。"},{"w":"seed drill","p":"n.","d":"a machine that plants seeds in neat rows","c":"播種機","s":"The farmer bought a new seed drill last spring, and now his seeds are planted at exactly the right depth in straight lines.","t":"這位農夫去年春天買了一台新的播種機，現在他的種子都能以剛好的深度種成整齊的直線。"},{"w":"hoe","p":"n.","d":"a garden tool with a long handle used to break up soil","c":"鋤頭","s":"My grandmother still uses an old hoe in her garden, and she says it is better exercise than going to the gym.","t":"我奶奶仍然在菜園裡用一把舊鋤頭，而且她說這比去健身房還要好的運動。"},{"w":"rake","p":"n.","d":"a tool with a row of teeth used to gather leaves or smooth soil","c":"耙子","s":"After the leaves fell in autumn, we used a rake to collect them, and then we added them to the compost pile.","t":"秋天落葉之後，我們用耙子把它們集中起來，然後加進堆肥堆裡。"},{"w":"sickle","p":"n.","d":"a curved blade with a short handle used for cutting crops","c":"鐮刀","s":"Before machines arrived, villagers cut rice with a sickle, and the work was so tiring that their backs ached for days.","t":"在機器出現之前，村民用鐮刀割稻，而且工作累到他們的背痛了好幾天。"},{"w":"silo","p":"n.","d":"a tall tower used for storing grain or animal food","c":"筒倉；穀倉塔","s":"The grain is kept in a huge silo next to the farm, because it stays dry there and rats cannot get inside.","t":"穀物存放在農場旁邊一座巨大的筒倉裡，因為那裡能保持乾燥，老鼠也進不去。"},{"w":"barn","p":"n.","d":"a large farm building for animals, crops or machines","c":"穀倉；畜舍","s":"The cows sleep in the barn during typhoons, and the farmer checks on them every few hours to make sure they are safe.","t":"颱風期間乳牛睡在畜舍裡，而且農夫每隔幾小時就去查看，確保牠們安全。"},{"w":"granary","p":"n.","d":"a building for storing grain","c":"糧倉","s":"In ancient times, every village had a granary for storing rice, so people would not starve if the next harvest failed.","t":"在古代，每個村莊都有一座糧倉來儲存稻米，所以即使下一次收成失敗，人們也不會挨餓。"},{"w":"furrow","p":"n.","d":"a long narrow line cut into soil for planting seeds","c":"犁溝；田溝","s":"The children dropped one seed into each furrow, and then they gently covered them with soil and gave them some water.","t":"孩子們在每一條田溝裡放一顆種子，然後輕輕蓋上泥土並澆一些水。"},{"w":"ditch","p":"n.","d":"a long narrow channel dug to carry water away","c":"水溝；溝渠","s":"The farmer dug a ditch along the edge of the field, so the heavy summer rain could drain away instead of flooding the crops.","t":"農夫沿著田邊挖了一條溝渠，所以夏天的大雨可以排掉，而不會淹沒作物。"},{"w":"hose","p":"n.","d":"a long rubber tube used to carry water","c":"水管","s":"I watered the vegetables with a hose this morning, but I forgot to turn it off, so the garden turned into a small lake.","t":"我今天早上用水管給蔬菜澆水，但我忘了關掉，所以菜園變成了一個小湖。"},{"w":"polytunnel","p":"n.","d":"a long plastic-covered tunnel for growing plants","c":"塑膠布棚（隧道式溫室）","s":"Many strawberry farms in Miaoli use a polytunnel to protect the fruit from rain, so visitors can still pick berries on wet days.","t":"苗栗許多草莓園使用塑膠布棚來保護果實不被雨淋，所以遊客即使在雨天也能採草莓。"},{"w":"pitchfork","p":"n.","d":"a tool with long metal points used to lift hay","c":"乾草叉","s":"The farmer lifted the hay with a pitchfork and threw it into the barn, while his dog ran around barking happily.","t":"農夫用乾草叉把乾草叉起來丟進穀倉，而他的狗在旁邊開心地跑來跑去吠叫。"},{"w":"trough","p":"n.","d":"a long open container for animals' food or water","c":"飼料槽；水槽","s":"Every morning the farmer fills the trough with fresh water, and the thirsty pigs push each other to drink first.","t":"每天早上農夫把水槽裝滿清水，而口渴的豬會互相推擠搶著先喝。"},{"w":"fertility","p":"n.","d":"the ability of land to produce good crops","c":"肥沃度；地力","s":"Volcanic ash can increase the fertility of the land, which is why farmers still grow crops near active volcanoes despite the danger.","t":"火山灰能提高土地的肥沃度，這就是為什麼儘管有危險，農民仍在活火山附近種植作物。"}]},{"unit":3,"theme":"Livestock & Animal Farming 畜牧與動物養殖","cards":[{"w":"dairy","p":"adj.","d":"made from milk, or connected with producing milk","c":"乳製品的；酪農的","s":"Cheese, yoghurt and butter are all dairy products, so people who cannot drink milk often have trouble eating them too.","t":"起司、優格和奶油都是乳製品，所以不能喝牛奶的人常常也很難吃這些東西。"},{"w":"pasture","p":"n.","d":"land covered with grass where animals feed","c":"牧場；牧草地","s":"The cows spend the day on the green pasture, and in the evening the farmer leads them back to the barn for milking.","t":"乳牛整天待在綠色的牧草地上，到了傍晚農夫再帶牠們回到牛舍擠奶。"},{"w":"meadow","p":"n.","d":"a field of grass and wild flowers","c":"草地；草原","s":"We had a picnic in a meadow full of wild flowers, but we had to leave quickly because a group of curious goats came over.","t":"我們在一片開滿野花的草地上野餐，但因為一群好奇的山羊跑了過來，我們只好趕快離開。"},{"w":"fodder","p":"n.","d":"food such as hay given to farm animals","c":"（家畜）飼料；草料","s":"The dry winter left little grass on the hills, so farmers had to buy fodder to keep their sheep alive.","t":"乾燥的冬天讓山坡上幾乎沒有草，所以農民必須購買草料來讓羊存活。"},{"w":"hay","p":"n.","d":"grass that has been cut and dried to feed animals","c":"乾草","s":"The farmers cut the grass in summer and dry it into hay, so the horses have enough food during the cold months.","t":"農民在夏天割草並曬成乾草，所以馬匹在寒冷的月份有足夠的食物。"},{"w":"silage","p":"n.","d":"green plants stored without air and used as animal food","c":"青貯飼料","s":"The farmer wraps the fresh grass in plastic to make silage, and the cows eat it happily all winter.","t":"農夫把新鮮的牧草用塑膠包起來做成青貯飼料，而乳牛整個冬天都吃得很開心。"},{"w":"pigsty","p":"n.","d":"a small building or area where pigs are kept","c":"豬圈","s":"The old pigsty behind the farmhouse was cleaned every day, but the smell still reached the neighbours when the wind blew.","t":"農舍後面的舊豬圈每天都會清理，但風一吹，臭味還是會飄到鄰居家。"},{"w":"chicken coop","p":"n.","d":"a small house where chickens are kept","c":"雞舍；雞籠","s":"We built a chicken coop in the backyard last year, and now we collect fresh eggs every morning before school.","t":"我們去年在後院蓋了一個雞舍，現在每天早上上學前都能撿到新鮮雞蛋。"},{"w":"battery cage","p":"n.","d":"a very small cage where egg-laying hens are kept","c":"層架式雞籠（格子籠）","s":"Hens in a battery cage cannot even spread their wings, so many shoppers now choose eggs from farms that let chickens walk around.","t":"關在格子籠裡的母雞連翅膀都無法張開，所以現在許多消費者選擇讓雞可以四處走動的農場所生產的雞蛋。"},{"w":"free-range","p":"adj.","d":"(of farm animals) allowed to move around outside","c":"放養的；放牧的","s":"free-range eggs cost a little more at the supermarket, but my mother buys them because she believes the hens live happier lives.","t":"放養雞蛋在超市貴一點，但我媽媽還是會買，因為她相信那些母雞過得比較快樂。"},{"w":"slaughterhouse","p":"n.","d":"a building where animals are killed for meat","c":"屠宰場","s":"The town's old slaughterhouse closed ten years ago, and it has now been turned into a cafe and art space.","t":"鎮上的舊屠宰場十年前關閉了，而它現在已經改建成咖啡廳和藝術空間。"},{"w":"slaughter","p":"v.","d":"to kill animals for food","c":"屠宰","s":"Farmers in the village used to slaughter a pig before Lunar New Year, and every family received some meat for the celebrations.","t":"村裡的農民以前會在農曆新年前屠宰一頭豬，而且每戶人家都能分到一些肉來過節。"},{"w":"butcher","p":"n.","d":"a person who cuts and sells meat","c":"肉販；屠夫","s":"The butcher at the morning market cuts the pork exactly the way my grandmother likes it, so she never buys meat anywhere else.","t":"早市的肉販會完全照我奶奶喜歡的方式切豬肉，所以她從不在別的地方買肉。"},{"w":"rear","p":"v.","d":"to look after animals until they are fully grown","c":"飼養；養育","s":"Their family has rear ducks in Yilan for many years, and their duck meat is famous all over the county.","t":"他們家在宜蘭養鴨已經很多年了，而且他們的鴨肉在全縣都很有名。"},{"w":"fatten","p":"v.","d":"to make an animal fat before it is killed for food","c":"養肥","s":"Some farmers fatten their cattle with corn for months, but grass-fed beef is becoming more popular because it is seen as healthier.","t":"有些農民用玉米把牛養肥好幾個月，但草飼牛肉越來越受歡迎，因為它被認為比較健康。"},{"w":"antibiotic","p":"n.","d":"a medicine that kills bacteria","c":"抗生素","s":"If farmers give animals an antibiotic too often, bacteria may become stronger, and medicines may stop working for humans too.","t":"如果農民太常給動物使用抗生素，細菌可能會變得更強，而藥物對人類也可能失效。"},{"w":"growth hormone","p":"n.","d":"a chemical that makes animals grow bigger faster","c":"生長激素","s":"Some countries allow farmers to give cattle growth hormone, but others have banned it because people worry about the effects on health.","t":"有些國家允許農民給牛使用生長激素，但其他國家已經禁止，因為人們擔心它對健康的影響。"},{"w":"animal welfare","p":"n.","d":"the health and comfort of animals","c":"動物福利","s":"The supermarket now sells eggs with an animal welfare label, so customers can see that the hens were treated kindly.","t":"這間超市現在販售貼有動物福利標章的雞蛋，所以顧客可以知道母雞受到善待。"},{"w":"factory farming","p":"n.","d":"keeping large numbers of animals indoors to produce cheap food","c":"工廠化養殖","s":"factory farming produces cheap meat for millions of people, but critics say the animals suffer because they have so little space.","t":"工廠化養殖為數百萬人生產便宜的肉品，但批評者說動物因為空間太小而受苦。"},{"w":"shear","p":"v.","d":"to cut the wool off a sheep","c":"剪（羊毛）","s":"The farmers shear the sheep every spring, so the animals stay cool in summer and the wool can be sold.","t":"農民每年春天替羊剪毛，所以羊在夏天能保持涼爽，羊毛也可以拿去賣。"},{"w":"fleece","p":"n.","d":"the wool coat of a sheep","c":"羊毛（整片）","s":"Each fleece was washed and dried in the sun, and then the women spun it into thread for warm winter sweaters.","t":"每一片羊毛都經過清洗並在陽光下曬乾，然後婦女們把它紡成線，用來織保暖的冬季毛衣。"},{"w":"hatchery","p":"n.","d":"a place where eggs are kept warm until young birds or fish come out","c":"孵化場","s":"The hatchery produces thousands of baby chickens every day, and they are sent to farms all over the island by truck.","t":"這座孵化場每天生產數千隻小雞，然後用卡車送到全島各地的農場。"},{"w":"broiler","p":"n.","d":"a young chicken raised for its meat","c":"肉雞","s":"A modern broiler grows so quickly that it is ready to sell in about six weeks, but some people think this is unnatural.","t":"現代的肉雞長得非常快，大約六週就可以出售，但有些人認為這很不自然。"},{"w":"beekeeping","p":"n.","d":"the work of keeping bees for honey","c":"養蜂","s":"My uncle took up beekeeping after he retired, and now he gives jars of honey to all his friends at Mid-Autumn Festival.","t":"我舅舅退休後開始養蜂，現在每到中秋節他都會送朋友們一罐罐蜂蜜。"},{"w":"beehive","p":"n.","d":"a box or structure where bees live and make honey","c":"蜂巢；蜂箱","s":"The farmer placed a beehive at the edge of the orchard, because the bees help the fruit trees and also produce honey.","t":"農夫在果園邊緣放了一個蜂箱，因為蜜蜂能幫助果樹授粉，也能生產蜂蜜。"},{"w":"milking machine","p":"n.","d":"a machine used to take milk from cows","c":"擠奶機","s":"The farm bought a milking machine last year, so the workers no longer get up at four o'clock to milk the cows by hand.","t":"這座農場去年買了一台擠奶機，所以工人不再需要凌晨四點起床用手擠牛奶。"},{"w":"ranch","p":"n.","d":"a very large farm for raising cattle, horses or sheep","c":"大牧場","s":"My cousin worked on a cattle ranch in Australia for a year, and he learned to ride a horse and fix fences.","t":"我表哥在澳洲的養牛大牧場工作了一年，而且學會了騎馬和修理圍籬。"},{"w":"lamb","p":"n.","d":"a young sheep, or its meat","c":"小羊；羊肉","s":"The newborn lamb could stand up within an hour, and the children watched quietly as it drank milk from its mother.","t":"這隻剛出生的小羊不到一小時就能站起來，孩子們靜靜地看著牠喝母羊的奶。"}]},{"unit":4,"theme":"Food Processing & Preservation 食品加工與保存","cards":[{"w":"processed food","p":"n.","d":"food changed by factory methods, often with added chemicals","c":"加工食品","s":"Instant noodles are a common processed food, and they are cheap and quick, but they often contain a lot of salt.","t":"泡麵是常見的加工食品，它們既便宜又快速，但常常含有大量的鹽。"},{"w":"ultra-processed","p":"adj.","d":"made mostly from factory ingredients rather than whole foods","c":"超加工的","s":"Many snacks in convenience stores are ultra-processed, so doctors advise teenagers to eat fruit and nuts instead.","t":"便利商店的許多零食都是超加工的，所以醫生建議青少年改吃水果和堅果。"},{"w":"preservative","p":"n.","d":"a chemical added to food to stop it from going bad","c":"防腐劑","s":"This bread contains no preservative, so it goes mouldy after three days, but my family thinks it tastes much fresher.","t":"這種麵包不含防腐劑，所以三天後就會發霉，但我們家覺得它吃起來新鮮多了。"},{"w":"additive","p":"n.","d":"a substance added to food to improve its colour, taste or life","c":"添加物","s":"The label lists every additive in the drink, but most customers do not read it because the words are very small.","t":"標籤上列出了飲料中的每一種添加物，但大多數顧客都不會去看，因為字實在太小了。"},{"w":"flavouring","p":"n.","d":"a substance added to food to give it a particular taste","c":"調味料；香料","s":"The strawberry milk contains no real fruit, only artificial flavouring, but children still love its sweet pink colour.","t":"這種草莓牛奶完全不含真的水果，只有人工香料，但孩子們還是很喜歡它甜甜的粉紅色。"},{"w":"sweetener","p":"n.","d":"a substance used instead of sugar to make food sweet","c":"甜味劑","s":"Diet cola uses an artificial sweetener instead of sugar, so it has almost no calories, but some people dislike the taste.","t":"無糖可樂使用人工甜味劑代替糖，所以幾乎沒有熱量，但有些人不喜歡它的味道。"},{"w":"emulsifier","p":"n.","d":"a substance that helps oil and water mix together","c":"乳化劑","s":"Ice cream often contains an emulsifier, because without it the cream and water would separate and the texture would become icy.","t":"冰淇淋常含有乳化劑，因為如果沒有它，奶油和水會分離，口感也會變得像冰渣。"},{"w":"pasteurise","p":"v.","d":"to heat milk or juice to kill harmful bacteria","c":"巴氏殺菌","s":"Dairy farms pasteurise milk before it goes to shops, because heating it kills bacteria that could make people sick.","t":"酪農場會在牛奶送到商店前先進行巴氏殺菌，因為加熱能殺死可能使人生病的細菌。"},{"w":"sterilise","p":"v.","d":"to make something completely free from bacteria","c":"消毒；殺菌","s":"My mother always sterilise the glass jars in boiling water before she makes jam, so the jam will not go bad.","t":"我媽媽做果醬前總會先把玻璃罐放進滾水中消毒，這樣果醬才不會壞掉。"},{"w":"freezer","p":"n.","d":"a machine or part of a fridge that keeps food frozen","c":"冷凍庫","s":"We keep dumplings in the freezer for busy evenings, and we can cook a quick dinner in ten minutes.","t":"我們把水餃放在冷凍庫裡備著忙碌的晚上吃，而且十分鐘就能煮好一頓快速的晚餐。"},{"w":"defrost","p":"v.","d":"to let frozen food become soft again","c":"解凍","s":"You should defrost the chicken in the fridge overnight, because leaving it on the table can allow bacteria to grow.","t":"你應該把雞肉放在冷藏室裡隔夜解凍，因為把它放在桌上可能會讓細菌滋生。"},{"w":"chilled","p":"adj.","d":"kept cold but not frozen","c":"冷藏的；冰鎮的","s":"chilled salads must stay below five degrees, so the delivery driver checks the temperature in his van every hour.","t":"冷藏沙拉必須保持在五度以下，所以送貨司機每小時都會檢查貨車內的溫度。"},{"w":"cold chain","p":"n.","d":"a system that keeps food cold from farm to shop","c":"冷鏈","s":"Vaccines and fresh fish both depend on the cold chain, because even a short break in cooling can make them unsafe.","t":"疫苗和鮮魚都仰賴冷鏈，因為即使冷藏只中斷一下，也可能讓它們變得不安全。"},{"w":"vacuum-packed","p":"adj.","d":"sealed in a pack with all the air removed","c":"真空包裝的","s":"The vacuum-packed meat stays fresh for weeks because no air can get in, so campers often take it on long trips.","t":"真空包裝的肉能保鮮好幾週，因為空氣進不去，所以露營者常帶著它去長途旅行。"},{"w":"airtight","p":"adj.","d":"not allowing air to get in or out","c":"密封的；不透氣的","s":"Keep the cookies in an airtight box, or they will become soft because of the wet weather in Taipei.","t":"把餅乾放在密封的盒子裡，否則它們會因為台北潮濕的天氣而變軟。"},{"w":"dehydrate","p":"v.","d":"to remove water from food to keep it longer","c":"使脫水；乾燥","s":"Factories dehydrate fruit to make healthy snacks, and the dried mango slices from Tainan are popular gifts for tourists.","t":"工廠將水果脫水製成健康的點心，而台南的芒果乾片是很受觀光客歡迎的伴手禮。"},{"w":"cure","p":"v.","d":"to keep meat or fish by drying, salting or smoking it","c":"醃製；燻製","s":"Families in the countryside cure pork with salt and spices before winter, so they have meat to eat during the holidays.","t":"鄉下的家庭會在冬天前用鹽和香料醃製豬肉，這樣過節時就有肉可吃。"},{"w":"pickle","p":"v.","d":"to keep food in vinegar or salt water","c":"醃漬","s":"My grandmother likes to pickle cucumbers in summer, and she keeps the jars in a cool cupboard for months.","t":"我奶奶喜歡在夏天醃漬小黃瓜，而且她把罐子放在陰涼的櫥櫃裡好幾個月。"},{"w":"ferment","p":"v.","d":"to change chemically because of bacteria or yeast","c":"發酵","s":"Cabbage is left to ferment for several days to make kimchi, and the bacteria give it a sour taste that many people love.","t":"高麗菜會放著發酵好幾天來做成泡菜，而細菌讓它產生許多人喜愛的酸味。"},{"w":"shelf life","p":"n.","d":"how long a product can be kept before it goes bad","c":"保存期限；架售期","s":"Canned soup has a long shelf life, so people often buy it before a typhoon, but fresh milk must be drunk within a week.","t":"罐頭湯的保存期限很長，所以人們常在颱風前購買，但鮮奶必須在一週內喝完。"},{"w":"best-before date","p":"n.","d":"the date until which food is at its best quality","c":"最佳賞味期限","s":"The yoghurt was two days past its best-before date, but it still smelled fine, so we decided to eat it.","t":"這罐優格已經過了最佳賞味期限兩天，但聞起來還是沒問題，所以我們決定把它吃掉。"},{"w":"spoil","p":"v.","d":"(of food) to become bad and unsafe to eat","c":"（食物）變質；壞掉","s":"Fresh fish can spoil within hours in summer, so the fishermen pack it in ice as soon as it is caught.","t":"新鮮的魚在夏天幾小時內就可能壞掉，所以漁夫一捕到魚就立刻用冰塊包裝。"},{"w":"rotten","p":"adj.","d":"old and bad, and no longer fit to eat","c":"腐爛的","s":"We found a rotten apple at the bottom of the bag, and it had already spoiled several others around it.","t":"我們在袋子底部發現了一顆腐爛的蘋果，而它已經把周圍好幾顆都弄壞了。"},{"w":"stale","p":"adj.","d":"(of bread or snacks) no longer fresh and becoming dry or hard","c":"不新鮮的；走味的","s":"The bread had gone stale because nobody closed the bag, so we fed it to the ducks in the park.","t":"因為沒有人把袋子封好，麵包變得不新鮮了，所以我們拿去公園餵鴨子。"},{"w":"perishable","p":"adj.","d":"likely to go bad quickly","c":"易腐壞的","s":"Strawberries are very perishable, so farmers have to sell them within a few days, or they will lose their money.","t":"草莓非常容易腐壞，所以農民必須在幾天內賣掉，否則就會虧錢。"},{"w":"flour","p":"n.","d":"powder made from grain and used for baking","c":"麵粉","s":"We mixed flour, eggs and milk to make pancakes, but the kitchen was covered in white powder by the time we finished.","t":"我們把麵粉、雞蛋和牛奶混在一起做鬆餅，但等我們做完時，廚房已經滿是白色粉末。"},{"w":"grind","p":"v.","d":"to crush something into small pieces or powder","c":"磨碎；研磨","s":"The cafe owner grinds the coffee beans just before he makes each cup, because he says it gives a much better smell.","t":"這位咖啡店老闆在沖每杯咖啡前才研磨咖啡豆，因為他說這樣香氣會好得多。"},{"w":"bottled","p":"adj.","d":"sold in bottles","c":"瓶裝的","s":"Many tourists buy bottled water every day, but the city now provides free water stations to cut down on plastic waste.","t":"許多觀光客每天都買瓶裝水，但這座城市現在提供免費飲水站來減少塑膠垃圾。"},{"w":"quick-freezing","p":"n.","d":"freezing food very fast to keep its taste and texture","c":"急速冷凍","s":"quick-freezing keeps vegetables bright and crunchy, because the ice crystals stay tiny and do not damage the cells.","t":"急速冷凍能讓蔬菜保持鮮豔和爽脆，因為冰晶很小，不會破壞細胞。"}]},{"unit":5,"theme":"Food Technology & Innovation 食品科技與創新","cards":[{"w":"food technology","p":"n.","d":"the science of making, storing and improving food","c":"食品科技","s":"Advances in food technology have made food safer and cheaper, but some people prefer traditional cooking because it feels more natural.","t":"食品科技的進步讓食物更安全也更便宜，但有些人比較喜歡傳統烹調，因為感覺比較天然。"},{"w":"food scientist","p":"n.","d":"a person who studies how food is made and kept safe","c":"食品科學家","s":"A food scientist tested the new sauce for months, and she changed the recipe because the colour faded too quickly.","t":"一位食品科學家花了好幾個月測試這款新醬料，她更改了配方，因為顏色褪得太快。"},{"w":"lab-grown meat","p":"n.","d":"meat made from animal cells in a laboratory","c":"實驗室培育肉","s":"lab-grown meat could reduce the number of animals that are killed, but it is still too expensive for most families to buy.","t":"實驗室培育肉可以減少被宰殺的動物數量，但對大多數家庭來說還是太貴了。"},{"w":"plant-based","p":"adj.","d":"made from plants rather than animals","c":"植物性的；以植物為原料的","s":"The burger shop now offers a plant-based burger, and many customers cannot tell the difference from beef.","t":"這家漢堡店現在提供植物性漢堡，而且許多顧客都吃不出它和牛肉的差別。"},{"w":"meat substitute","p":"n.","d":"a food that is used instead of meat","c":"肉類替代品","s":"Tofu has been a popular meat substitute in Asia for centuries, so new plant-based products are not really a new idea here.","t":"豆腐在亞洲作為肉類替代品已經流行了好幾個世紀，所以新的植物性產品在這裡其實不算新點子。"},{"w":"alternative protein","p":"n.","d":"a source of protein other than traditional meat","c":"替代蛋白質","s":"Investors are spending billions on alternative protein because the world's population is growing, and farms cannot produce enough meat for everyone.","t":"投資人在替代蛋白質上投入數十億元，因為世界人口持續成長，而農場無法生產足夠所有人吃的肉。"},{"w":"edible insect","p":"n.","d":"an insect that is safe for people to eat","c":"可食用昆蟲","s":"Crickets are an edible insect that is rich in protein, but many people in Taiwan still feel nervous about tasting them.","t":"蟋蟀是一種富含蛋白質的可食用昆蟲，但許多台灣人對品嘗牠們仍然感到緊張。"},{"w":"genetically modified","p":"adj.","d":"having genes changed by scientists","c":"基因改造的","s":"Most of the soybeans that Taiwan imports are genetically modified, so tofu makers must label clearly which products use them.","t":"台灣進口的黃豆大多是基因改造的，所以豆腐業者必須清楚標示哪些產品有使用。"},{"w":"GMO","p":"n.","d":"a living thing whose genes have been changed by science","c":"基因改造生物","s":"School lunches in Taiwan cannot contain any GMO, because parents asked the government to make this rule several years ago.","t":"台灣的學校午餐不能含有任何基因改造生物，因為家長幾年前要求政府訂定這項規定。"},{"w":"gene editing","p":"n.","d":"changing the DNA of a living thing in a precise way","c":"基因編輯","s":"Scientists are using gene editing to create rice that survives floods, and farmers in Asia hope it will protect their harvests.","t":"科學家正在運用基因編輯培育能在洪水中存活的稻米，而亞洲的農民希望它能保護他們的收成。"},{"w":"biotechnology","p":"n.","d":"using living cells and bacteria to make useful products","c":"生物科技","s":"My sister wants to study biotechnology at university, because she believes it can help farmers grow food with fewer chemicals.","t":"我姊姊想在大學攻讀生物科技，因為她相信它能幫助農民用更少的化學物質種植糧食。"},{"w":"hydroponics","p":"n.","d":"growing plants in water with nutrients instead of soil","c":"水耕栽培","s":"The restaurant grows its own lettuce using hydroponics, so it needs no soil, and the leaves are picked just before serving.","t":"這家餐廳用水耕栽培自己種萵苣，所以不需要土壤，而且葉子是上菜前才採下的。"},{"w":"aquaponics","p":"n.","d":"a system where fish and plants are raised together in water","c":"魚菜共生","s":"Our school built an aquaponics system in the science lab, and the students feed the fish while the plants clean the water.","t":"我們學校在科學實驗室裡建造了一套魚菜共生系統，學生餵魚，而植物則負責淨化水質。"},{"w":"vertical farming","p":"n.","d":"growing crops in stacked layers, often inside buildings","c":"垂直農法","s":"vertical farming allows cities to produce vegetables in tall buildings, but the lights use a lot of electricity, so costs remain high.","t":"垂直農法讓城市能在高樓裡生產蔬菜，但照明耗電量很大，所以成本仍然很高。"},{"w":"indoor farm","p":"n.","d":"a farm inside a building with controlled light and temperature","c":"室內農場","s":"The indoor farm near the train station grows herbs all year round, and typhoons cannot damage the crops because they are inside.","t":"火車站附近的室內農場全年都在種植香草，而且颱風也無法破壞作物，因為它們都在室內。"},{"w":"precision agriculture","p":"n.","d":"farming that uses data and technology to treat each part of a field correctly","c":"精準農業","s":"With precision agriculture, farmers use drones and sensors to find dry areas, so they only water the plants that really need it.","t":"透過精準農業，農民使用無人機和感測器找出乾燥的區域，所以他們只澆灌真正需要水的植物。"},{"w":"agritech","p":"n.","d":"technology used to improve farming","c":"農業科技","s":"Young engineers are starting agritech companies in Taiwan, and they hope their apps will help older farmers save time and water.","t":"年輕工程師在台灣創立農業科技公司，而他們希望自己的應用程式能幫助年長的農民節省時間和水。"},{"w":"smart farming","p":"n.","d":"farming with connected devices that collect and share data","c":"智慧農業","s":"smart farming lets my uncle check the temperature of his greenhouse on his phone, so he can relax even when he travels.","t":"智慧農業讓我叔叔能用手機查看溫室的溫度，所以他即使出門旅行也能放心。"},{"w":"high-yield","p":"adj.","d":"producing a large amount of crops","c":"高產量的","s":"Scientists developed high-yield rice in the 1960s, and it helped millions of people in Asia escape hunger.","t":"科學家在1960年代培育出高產量的稻米，而它幫助亞洲數百萬人擺脫飢餓。"},{"w":"hybrid","p":"n.","d":"a plant or animal produced from two different types","c":"雜交種；混種","s":"This papaya is a hybrid of two local types, so it is both sweet and strong enough to survive the windy season.","t":"這種木瓜是兩個本地品種的雜交種，所以它既甜又強壯，能撐過多風的季節。"},{"w":"seed bank","p":"n.","d":"a place where seeds are stored to protect plant varieties","c":"種子庫","s":"A seed bank in Norway keeps millions of seeds deep inside a mountain, so crops can be replanted if a disaster happens.","t":"挪威的一座種子庫將數百萬顆種子保存在山的深處，所以如果發生災難，作物就能重新種植。"},{"w":"Green Revolution","p":"n.","d":"the rapid rise in crop production in the 1960s using new seeds and chemicals","c":"綠色革命","s":"The Green Revolution doubled rice harvests in many countries, but it also increased the use of chemicals and water.","t":"綠色革命讓許多國家的稻米收成加倍，但它也增加了化學物質和水的使用量。"},{"w":"agrochemical","p":"n.","d":"a chemical used in farming, such as a fertiliser or pesticide","c":"農用化學品","s":"The company sells every kind of agrochemical to farmers, but it is also developing natural products because customers want safer food.","t":"這家公司向農民銷售各種農用化學品，但它也在研發天然產品，因為消費者想要更安全的食物。"},{"w":"mycoprotein","p":"n.","d":"protein made from a type of fungus, used instead of meat","c":"真菌蛋白","s":"The vegetarian nuggets are made from mycoprotein, and they taste surprisingly like chicken, so even my meat-loving father enjoyed them.","t":"這款素雞塊是用真菌蛋白做的，而且吃起來出奇地像雞肉，所以連愛吃肉的爸爸都很喜歡。"},{"w":"superfood","p":"n.","d":"a food said to be especially good for your health","c":"超級食物","s":"Blueberries are often called a superfood, but nutritionists say that a balanced diet matters more than any single fruit.","t":"藍莓常被稱為超級食物，但營養師說均衡飲食比任何單一水果都更重要。"},{"w":"3D food printing","p":"n.","d":"making food in shapes using a machine that builds it in layers","c":"3D食物列印","s":"The hotel used 3D food printing to make chocolate in the shape of Taipei 101, and the guests took photos before they ate it.","t":"這家飯店運用3D食物列印做出台北101形狀的巧克力，客人在吃之前都先拍了照。"},{"w":"meal kit","p":"n.","d":"a box of ingredients and a recipe delivered to your home","c":"料理包；食材組","s":"My parents order a meal kit every week because they are busy, and all the ingredients arrive already measured.","t":"我爸媽因為很忙，每週都會訂一盒食材組，而且所有食材送來時都已經量好了。"},{"w":"food delivery app","p":"n.","d":"a phone app used to order meals to your home","c":"外送應用程式","s":"Students often use a food delivery app late at night, but the plastic boxes create a lot of rubbish.","t":"學生常在深夜使用外送應用程式，但塑膠餐盒製造了大量垃圾。"},{"w":"bioreactor","p":"n.","d":"a large tank where cells or bacteria are grown","c":"生物反應器","s":"The meat cells grow inside a steel bioreactor for several weeks, and scientists control the temperature very carefully.","t":"肉類細胞在鋼製的生物反應器裡生長好幾個星期，而科學家會非常小心地控制溫度。"}]},{"unit":6,"theme":"Nutrition, Diet & Food Safety 營養、飲食與食品安全","cards":[{"w":"nutrition","p":"n.","d":"the food you eat and how it affects your health","c":"營養","s":"Good nutrition is important for teenagers because they are still growing, so schools try to serve balanced lunches.","t":"良好的營養對青少年很重要，因為他們還在成長，所以學校努力提供均衡的午餐。"},{"w":"nutritious","p":"adj.","d":"full of things that are good for your body","c":"有營養的","s":"Sweet potatoes are cheap and nutritious, so my grandmother says they helped many families survive during hard times.","t":"地瓜既便宜又有營養，所以我奶奶說它在艱困時期幫助許多家庭活了下來。"},{"w":"nutritionist","p":"n.","d":"an expert on food and healthy eating","c":"營養師","s":"The school nutritionist plans the lunch menu every month, and she makes sure there are vegetables in every meal.","t":"學校的營養師每個月規劃午餐菜單，而且她確保每一餐都有蔬菜。"},{"w":"balanced diet","p":"n.","d":"eating the right amounts of different kinds of food","c":"均衡飲食","s":"A balanced diet includes fruit, vegetables, grains and protein, so you should not live on fried chicken and bubble tea.","t":"均衡飲食包括水果、蔬菜、穀物和蛋白質，所以你不應該只靠炸雞和珍珠奶茶過活。"},{"w":"protein","p":"n.","d":"a nutrient in meat, eggs and beans that builds muscles","c":"蛋白質","s":"Athletes need plenty of protein to build muscle, so many of them eat eggs, chicken or tofu after training.","t":"運動員需要大量的蛋白質來增加肌肉，所以他們許多人在訓練後吃雞蛋、雞肉或豆腐。"},{"w":"carbohydrate","p":"n.","d":"a nutrient in rice, bread and noodles that gives energy","c":"碳水化合物","s":"Rice is the main carbohydrate in many Asian meals, and it gives students the energy they need for long school days.","t":"米飯是許多亞洲餐點中主要的碳水化合物，而且它提供學生漫長上學日所需的能量。"},{"w":"fibre","p":"n.","d":"the part of plant food that helps digestion","c":"纖維","s":"Brown rice contains more fibre than white rice, so it keeps you full for longer and helps your stomach work well.","t":"糙米比白米含有更多纖維，所以能讓你飽得更久，也能幫助腸胃正常運作。"},{"w":"vitamin","p":"n.","d":"a natural substance in food that the body needs to stay healthy","c":"維他命；維生素","s":"Oranges are full of vitamin C, so my mother makes us eat one every day when it is flu season.","t":"柳橙富含維他命C，所以在流感季節我媽媽每天都要我們吃一顆。"},{"w":"calorie","p":"n.","d":"a unit for measuring the energy in food","c":"卡路里；熱量","s":"One cup of bubble tea can contain more than five hundred calorie, so it is almost like eating a whole meal.","t":"一杯珍珠奶茶可能含有超過五百卡路里，所以幾乎就像吃了一整餐。"},{"w":"sodium","p":"n.","d":"a chemical in salt that can be unhealthy in large amounts","c":"鈉","s":"Instant noodles are very high in sodium, so doctors warn that eating them often may raise your blood pressure.","t":"泡麵的鈉含量非常高，所以醫生警告常吃可能會讓血壓升高。"},{"w":"cholesterol","p":"n.","d":"a fatty substance in the blood that can block blood vessels","c":"膽固醇","s":"My father's cholesterol was too high last year, so he stopped eating fried food and started jogging every morning.","t":"我爸爸去年膽固醇太高，所以他不再吃油炸食物，並開始每天早上慢跑。"},{"w":"obesity","p":"n.","d":"the state of being very overweight","c":"肥胖（症）","s":"Childhood obesity is rising in many countries, and experts blame sugary drinks as well as too much time on screens.","t":"兒童肥胖在許多國家持續增加，而專家將原因歸咎於含糖飲料以及花太多時間在螢幕上。"},{"w":"food poisoning","p":"n.","d":"illness caused by eating food that contains harmful bacteria","c":"食物中毒","s":"Several students got food poisoning after the school trip, and the health department later found that the lunch boxes had been left in the sun.","t":"好幾個學生在校外教學後食物中毒，而衛生局後來發現便當被放在太陽底下曬。"},{"w":"salmonella","p":"n.","d":"a type of bacteria that causes food poisoning","c":"沙門氏菌","s":"Raw eggs may carry salmonella, so you should cook them properly, especially when you serve them to children.","t":"生雞蛋可能帶有沙門氏菌，所以你應該把蛋煮熟，尤其是給小孩吃的時候。"},{"w":"food safety","p":"n.","d":"keeping food free from things that can make people ill","c":"食品安全","s":"After several scandals about cooking oil, food safety became a major concern in Taiwan, and the government made stricter rules.","t":"在幾起食用油醜聞之後，食品安全成為台灣重大的關注議題，而政府也訂定了更嚴格的規定。"},{"w":"food inspector","p":"n.","d":"an official who checks that food and restaurants are safe","c":"食品稽查員","s":"A food inspector visited the night market last week, and two stalls were fined because their kitchens were dirty.","t":"上週一名食品稽查員到夜市檢查，而有兩個攤位因為廚房骯髒而被罰款。"},{"w":"nutrition label","p":"n.","d":"information on a food package about its nutrients","c":"營養標示","s":"Check the nutrition label on the back of the box, and you will see how much sugar is hidden in this healthy-looking cereal.","t":"看看盒子背面的營養標示，你就會發現這款看起來很健康的穀片裡藏了多少糖。"},{"w":"allergen","p":"n.","d":"a substance that causes an allergic reaction","c":"過敏原","s":"Peanuts are a common allergen, so restaurants must tell customers if any dish contains them.","t":"花生是常見的過敏原，所以餐廳必須告知顧客是否有任何菜餚含有花生。"},{"w":"gluten-free","p":"adj.","d":"not containing gluten, a protein found in wheat","c":"無麩質的","s":"The bakery started selling gluten-free bread last year, and it quickly became popular with customers who cannot eat wheat.","t":"這家麵包店去年開始販售無麩質麵包，而且很快就受到不能吃小麥的顧客歡迎。"},{"w":"vegan","p":"n.","d":"a person who eats no animal products at all","c":"純素食者","s":"My cousin became a vegan last year, so she no longer eats meat, eggs or milk, but she still loves cooking for her friends.","t":"我表妹去年成為純素食者，所以她不再吃肉、蛋或牛奶，但她仍然很喜歡為朋友下廚。"},{"w":"vegetarian","p":"n.","d":"a person who does not eat meat or fish","c":"素食者","s":"Taiwan is an easy place for a vegetarian to travel, because there are vegetarian restaurants in almost every neighbourhood.","t":"台灣對素食者來說是很容易旅行的地方，因為幾乎每個社區都有素食餐廳。"},{"w":"wholegrain","p":"adj.","d":"made with the whole seed of the grain, including the outer layer","c":"全穀的","s":"wholegrain bread is healthier than white bread, but my little brother refuses to eat it because he says it tastes like cardboard.","t":"全穀麵包比白麵包健康，但我弟弟拒絕吃，因為他說吃起來像紙板。"},{"w":"junk food","p":"n.","d":"food that is tasty but unhealthy","c":"垃圾食物","s":"I try not to eat junk food before exams, but chips and chocolate are hard to resist when I study late.","t":"我考試前盡量不吃垃圾食物，但熬夜讀書時，洋芋片和巧克力實在很難抗拒。"},{"w":"serving size","p":"n.","d":"the amount of food that counts as one portion on a label","c":"每份份量","s":"The serving size on the snack bag is only ten chips, but most people eat the whole bag in one go.","t":"零食袋上標示的每份份量只有十片洋芋片，但大多數人一口氣就吃掉整包。"},{"w":"undercooked","p":"adj.","d":"not cooked long enough","c":"未煮熟的","s":"The chicken was undercooked in the middle, so we sent it back to the kitchen because we did not want to get sick.","t":"雞肉中間沒有煮熟，所以我們把它退回廚房，因為我們不想生病。"},{"w":"food handler","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job involves preparing or serving food","c":"食品從業人員","s":"Every food handler must wear gloves and a hat, and they need a health check before they start working in the kitchen.","t":"每位食品從業人員都必須戴手套和帽子，而且他們在進廚房工作前需要接受健康檢查。"},{"w":"digest","p":"v.","d":"to break down food in the stomach so the body can use it","c":"消化","s":"Some adults cannot digest milk easily, so they feel uncomfortable after drinking a latte, but they can still eat cheese.","t":"有些成人不容易消化牛奶，所以喝完拿鐵後會不舒服，但他們仍然可以吃起司。"},{"w":"sugary","p":"adj.","d":"containing a lot of sugar","c":"含糖量高的；含糖的","s":"The government wants to tax sugary drinks, because they are a major cause of tooth decay and weight problems among children.","t":"政府想對含糖飲料課稅，因為它們是兒童蛀牙和體重問題的主要原因。"},{"w":"dietary","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the food people eat","c":"飲食的","s":"The hotel asks every guest about their dietary needs, so the chef can prepare meals without nuts, meat or wheat.","t":"這家飯店會詢問每位客人的飲食需求，所以主廚可以準備不含堅果、肉或小麥的餐點。"}]},{"unit":7,"theme":"Food Supply, Trade & Waste 糧食供應、貿易與浪費","cards":[{"w":"food supply","p":"n.","d":"the amount of food available to a population","c":"糧食供應","s":"The war cut off the city's food supply, so prices rose quickly and many families could only afford one meal a day.","t":"戰爭切斷了這座城市的糧食供應，所以物價迅速上漲，許多家庭一天只吃得起一餐。"},{"w":"food shortage","p":"n.","d":"a situation in which there is not enough food","c":"糧食短缺","s":"The drought caused a serious food shortage in the region, and international groups sent rice and flour to help.","t":"乾旱在該地區造成嚴重的糧食短缺，而國際組織送來了稻米和麵粉協助。"},{"w":"hunger","p":"n.","d":"the state of not having enough food to eat","c":"飢餓","s":"Millions of people still suffer from hunger every day, although the world produces enough food for everyone.","t":"每天仍有數百萬人遭受飢餓之苦，儘管全世界生產的糧食足夠每個人吃。"},{"w":"grocery","p":"n.","d":"food and other goods sold in a shop","c":"食品雜貨","s":"We do our grocery shopping on Sunday mornings, because the market is less crowded and the vegetables are fresh.","t":"我們都在星期天早上採買食品雜貨，因為市場人比較少，而且蔬菜很新鮮。"},{"w":"supermarket","p":"n.","d":"a large shop that sells food and household goods","c":"超市","s":"The supermarket near my home sells vegetables from local farms, and the farmers' names and photos are printed on the packets.","t":"我家附近的超市販售本地農場的蔬菜，而且包裝上印著農民的名字和照片。"},{"w":"wholesaler","p":"n.","d":"a business that sells large amounts of goods to shops","c":"批發商","s":"Farmers sell their cabbages to a wholesaler, and he then sells them to restaurants and markets around the city.","t":"農民把高麗菜賣給一位批發商，然後他再把它們賣給市區各地的餐廳和市場。"},{"w":"middleman","p":"n.","d":"a person who buys from producers and sells to shops or customers","c":"中間商；中盤商","s":"Farmers often earn very little because the middleman takes a large share of the profit, so some now sell directly online.","t":"農民常常賺得很少，因為中間商拿走大部分利潤，所以現在有些人直接在網路上販售。"},{"w":"farmers' market","p":"n.","d":"a market where farmers sell their own produce directly","c":"農夫市集","s":"Every Saturday there is a farmers' market near the park, and you can talk to the people who actually grew your vegetables.","t":"每週六公園附近都有農夫市集，而且你可以和親手種出你蔬菜的人聊天。"},{"w":"produce","p":"n.","d":"fruit and vegetables grown for sale","c":"農產品","s":"Fresh produce from the mountains arrives at the market early in the morning, so chefs go there before sunrise to choose the best.","t":"來自山區的新鮮農產品一大早就送到市場，所以廚師們在日出前就去挑選最好的。"},{"w":"food miles","p":"n.","d":"the distance food travels from where it is grown to where it is eaten","c":"食物里程","s":"Buying local fruit reduces food miles, because it does not have to be flown across the world before it reaches your table.","t":"購買本地水果能減少食物里程，因為它不必飛越半個地球才送上你的餐桌。"},{"w":"fair trade","p":"n.","d":"a system that pays farmers in poor countries a fair price","c":"公平貿易","s":"This coffee is sold under fair trade, so the farmers in Africa receive a fair price and can send their children to school.","t":"這款咖啡以公平貿易方式販售，所以非洲的農民能得到合理的價格，並送孩子上學。"},{"w":"rationing","p":"n.","d":"limiting the amount of food each person may have","c":"配給（制度）","s":"During the war, food rationing meant that each family could buy only a little sugar and meat each week.","t":"戰爭期間，糧食配給代表每個家庭每週只能買一點點糖和肉。"},{"w":"food bank","p":"n.","d":"a place that gives free food to people in need","c":"食物銀行","s":"Our class collected canned food for the local food bank, and the volunteers gave it to families who could not afford groceries.","t":"我們班為當地的食物銀行收集罐頭食品，而志工把它們送給買不起食物的家庭。"},{"w":"food waste","p":"n.","d":"food that is thrown away instead of eaten","c":"食物浪費；廚餘","s":"Restaurants produce a lot of food waste every night, so some now give unsold bread to charities instead of throwing it away.","t":"餐廳每晚都產生大量廚餘，所以現在有些餐廳把沒賣完的麵包捐給慈善機構，而不是丟掉。"},{"w":"leftovers","p":"n.","d":"food that remains after a meal","c":"剩菜","s":"We often eat the leftovers from Sunday dinner for lunch on Monday, so nothing goes to waste in our house.","t":"我們常把星期天晚餐的剩菜當作星期一的午餐，所以我們家沒有東西會浪費。"},{"w":"imperfect","p":"adj.","d":"(of fruit or vegetables) not perfect in shape or appearance","c":"不完美的；賣相不佳的","s":"The supermarket sells imperfect carrots at half price, and customers have discovered that they taste just as good.","t":"這家超市以半價販售賣相不佳的紅蘿蔔，而顧客們發現它們吃起來一樣美味。"},{"w":"food aid","p":"n.","d":"food given to countries or people in need","c":"糧食援助","s":"After the earthquake, food aid arrived from many countries, but the broken roads made it hard to reach mountain villages.","t":"地震後，來自許多國家的糧食援助抵達了，但損毀的道路讓物資很難送到山區村莊。"},{"w":"grain reserve","p":"n.","d":"a store of grain kept for emergencies","c":"儲備糧","s":"The government keeps a large grain reserve of rice, so prices stay stable even when typhoons destroy part of the harvest.","t":"政府保有大量的稻米儲備糧，所以即使颱風摧毀部分收成，價格也能保持穩定。"},{"w":"crop insurance","p":"n.","d":"insurance that pays farmers if their harvest is damaged","c":"農作物保險","s":"My uncle bought crop insurance for his banana farm, and it paid for most of his losses when the typhoon hit.","t":"我叔叔為他的香蕉園買了農作物保險，而颱風來襲時，它賠償了他大部分的損失。"},{"w":"agribusiness","p":"n.","d":"farming run as a large industry","c":"農業企業；農產綜合企業","s":"Large agribusiness companies control much of the world's seed market, so small farmers often worry about rising prices.","t":"大型農業企業控制了全球大部分的種子市場，所以小農常擔心價格上漲。"},{"w":"distributor","p":"n.","d":"a company that delivers goods from producers to shops","c":"經銷商","s":"The milk distributor delivers to over two hundred stores every morning, so his trucks leave the factory before dawn.","t":"這家牛奶經銷商每天早上配送到兩百多家商店，所以他的貨車天亮前就離開工廠。"},{"w":"refrigerated truck","p":"n.","d":"a truck with a cooling system for carrying fresh food","c":"冷藏車","s":"The fish is carried in a refrigerated truck from the port to Taipei, and the temperature inside is checked throughout the journey.","t":"魚貨用冷藏車從港口運到台北，而且一路上都會檢查車內的溫度。"},{"w":"cold storage","p":"n.","d":"keeping food in a cold place so it stays fresh","c":"冷藏庫；冷藏儲存","s":"Apples can be kept in cold storage for many months, so we can buy them all year, although they are picked only in autumn.","t":"蘋果可以在冷藏庫裡保存好幾個月，所以儘管只在秋天採收，我們卻能全年買到。"},{"w":"price hike","p":"n.","d":"a sudden large increase in price","c":"漲價","s":"After the typhoon there was a big price hike for vegetables, so many families ate more tofu and eggs that week.","t":"颱風過後蔬菜大幅漲價，所以那週許多家庭都多吃豆腐和雞蛋。"},{"w":"bulk buying","p":"n.","d":"buying large amounts at one time, usually at a lower price","c":"大量採購","s":"bulk buying can save money for big families, but food may go bad if you buy more than you can eat.","t":"大量採購可以為大家庭省錢，但如果你買的比吃得完的還多，食物就可能壞掉。"},{"w":"retailer","p":"n.","d":"a business that sells goods directly to the public","c":"零售商","s":"The retailer promised to stop selling eggs from caged hens by 2030, and other shops soon made the same promise.","t":"這家零售商承諾在2030年前停止販售籠飼雞蛋，而其他商店很快也做出了同樣的承諾。"},{"w":"food scraps","p":"n.","d":"small pieces of leftover food that are thrown away","c":"廚餘碎屑","s":"In Taipei we put food scraps in a special bin, and the city turns them into pig feed or fertiliser.","t":"在台北我們把廚餘放進專用的桶子，而市政府會把它們變成豬飼料或肥料。"},{"w":"doggy bag","p":"n.","d":"a bag or box for taking home food you did not finish at a restaurant","c":"打包袋（剩菜外帶）","s":"We could not finish the huge pizza, so we asked the waiter for a doggy bag and took the rest home for breakfast.","t":"我們吃不完那個超大披薩，所以我們跟服務生要了打包袋，把剩下的帶回家當早餐。"}]},{"unit":8,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 1 (acclimatise – coarse)","cards":[{"w":"acclimatise","p":"v.","d":"to get used to a new climate or situation","c":"適應（新環境）","s":"The new rice variety needed two seasons to acclimatise to the cooler mountain weather, but now it grows as well as it does on the plains.","t":"這個新稻種花了兩季才適應較涼的山區天氣，但現在它長得跟在平原上一樣好。"},{"w":"adulterate","p":"v.","d":"to make food worse by adding cheaper or harmful things","c":"摻假；摻雜","s":"Some dishonest companies adulterate honey with cheap sugar syrup, so experts test samples in the lab before they reach shops.","t":"有些不肖公司用便宜的糖漿摻假蜂蜜，所以專家會在樣品進入商店前先在實驗室檢驗。"},{"w":"affordability","p":"n.","d":"how cheap enough something is for people to buy","c":"可負擔性","s":"The affordability of fresh vegetables has become a problem since the typhoon, and many families now buy frozen ones instead.","t":"颱風過後，新鮮蔬菜的可負擔性成了問題，而許多家庭現在改買冷凍蔬菜。"},{"w":"allure","p":"n.","d":"the attractive or exciting quality of something","c":"吸引力；魅力","s":"The allure of city jobs draws young people away from farming villages, so many fields are now looked after by elderly farmers.","t":"城市工作的吸引力讓年輕人離開農村，所以現在許多田地都由年長的農民照料。"},{"w":"ambiguity","p":"n.","d":"the state of having more than one possible meaning","c":"模稜兩可；含糊","s":"There is some ambiguity in the word 'natural' on food labels, so shoppers may think a product is healthier than it really is.","t":"食品標籤上「天然」這個詞有些模稜兩可，所以消費者可能以為產品比實際更健康。"},{"w":"annihilate","p":"v.","d":"to destroy something completely","c":"徹底摧毀；殲滅","s":"A swarm of locusts can annihilate a whole field of wheat in a single day, and farmers can do almost nothing to stop it.","t":"一大群蝗蟲能在一天之內徹底摧毀整片麥田，而農民幾乎束手無策。"},{"w":"anomalous","p":"adj.","d":"different from what is normal or expected","c":"異常的；反常的","s":"The scientists found anomalous levels of chemicals in the river near the farm, so they took more samples to check the results.","t":"科學家在農場附近的河流中發現異常的化學物質含量，所以他們採集更多樣本來確認結果。"},{"w":"antidote","p":"n.","d":"something that reduces the bad effects of another thing","c":"解藥；矯正方法","s":"Home cooking can be an antidote to fast-food culture, and it also gives families a chance to talk at the dinner table.","t":"在家做飯可以是速食文化的解藥，而且它也讓家人有機會在餐桌上聊天。"},{"w":"apportion","p":"v.","d":"to divide something and share it out","c":"分配；分攤","s":"The village committee had to apportion the limited water between the farms, but every farmer believed he deserved more.","t":"村委會必須把有限的水分配給各個農場，但每位農民都認為自己應該分到更多。"},{"w":"aspiration","p":"n.","d":"a strong hope to achieve something","c":"抱負；志向","s":"Her aspiration is to run an organic farm in Hualien, so she is studying soil science and saving money every month.","t":"她的志向是在花蓮經營一座有機農場，所以她正在研讀土壤科學，並且每個月存錢。"},{"w":"assimilate","p":"v.","d":"to take in and fully understand information or ideas","c":"吸收；理解","s":"Young farmers assimilate new technology quickly, while older farmers often need more time and practical examples.","t":"年輕農民很快就能吸收新科技，而年長的農民常需要更多時間和實際例子。"},{"w":"astounding","p":"adj.","d":"very surprising or shocking","c":"令人震驚的；驚人的","s":"The amount of food wasted every year is astounding, and one third of all food never reaches anyone's mouth.","t":"每年浪費的食物量驚人，而所有食物中有三分之一從來沒有被吃進任何人的嘴裡。"},{"w":"attainable","p":"adj.","d":"possible to achieve","c":"可達成的","s":"The goal of halving food waste is attainable, but only if shops, restaurants and families all change their habits.","t":"將食物浪費減半的目標是可以達成的，但前提是商店、餐廳和家庭都要改變習慣。"},{"w":"austerity","p":"n.","d":"a situation in which people have less money and must spend carefully","c":"撙節；緊縮","s":"During the years of austerity, many families grew vegetables in their gardens, and they rarely ate in restaurants.","t":"在撙節的那些年，許多家庭在院子裡種菜，而且他們很少上館子吃飯。"},{"w":"authenticity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being real or true","c":"真實性；道地","s":"Customers question the authenticity of 'local' honey that is sold so cheaply, and some samples turned out to be imported.","t":"顧客質疑那些賣得如此便宜的「本地」蜂蜜的真實性，而有些樣本後來證實是進口的。"},{"w":"averse","p":"adj.","d":"strongly disliking or not wanting something","c":"反對的；不願意的","s":"Many older farmers are averse to taking risks, so they keep growing the same crops that their parents grew.","t":"許多年長的農民不願意冒險，所以他們繼續種植父母那一代所種的作物。"},{"w":"backbone","p":"n.","d":"the most important part that supports a system","c":"支柱；骨幹","s":"Small family farms are the backbone of the local economy, so the closing of even one farm affects the whole village.","t":"小型家庭農場是當地經濟的支柱，所以即使只有一座農場關閉，也會影響整個村莊。"},{"w":"belated","p":"adj.","d":"happening or coming later than it should","c":"延遲的；遲來的","s":"The government made a belated attempt to help the banana farmers, but by then many of them had already lost their land.","t":"政府遲來地嘗試幫助香蕉農，但那時他們許多人已經失去了土地。"},{"w":"beneficiary","p":"n.","d":"a person who gets an advantage from something","c":"受益者","s":"The main beneficiary of the new irrigation system was the village school, because it could finally grow its own vegetables.","t":"新灌溉系統的主要受益者是村裡的學校，因為它終於能種自己的蔬菜了。"},{"w":"bountiful","p":"adj.","d":"in large amounts; plentiful","c":"豐富的；大量的","s":"The rain came at the right time this year, so the harvest was bountiful and the farmers held a big festival.","t":"今年雨水來得正是時候，所以收成豐碩，而農民們舉辦了一場盛大的慶典。"},{"w":"cascade","p":"n.","d":"a series of things that happen one after another","c":"一連串；連鎖","s":"The drought caused a cascade of problems, because crops failed, food prices rose and many workers lost their jobs.","t":"乾旱引發了一連串的問題，因為作物歉收、糧價上漲，許多工人也失去了工作。"},{"w":"catastrophe","p":"n.","d":"a sudden event that causes great damage","c":"大災難","s":"A failed rice harvest would be a catastrophe for the region, so scientists are working hard on flood-resistant seeds.","t":"稻米歉收對這個地區會是一場大災難，所以科學家正努力研發耐洪水的種子。"},{"w":"cessation","p":"n.","d":"the stopping of something","c":"停止；中止","s":"The cessation of fighting allowed farmers to return to their fields, and food began to reach the markets again.","t":"戰事的停止讓農民得以回到田裡，而食物也開始重新送到市場。"},{"w":"clandestine","p":"adj.","d":"secret and often illegal","c":"祕密的；暗中的","s":"Police discovered a clandestine factory that was making fake cooking oil, and it had been selling to night markets for years.","t":"警方發現了一家祕密製造假食用油的工廠，而且它已經賣給夜市好幾年了。"},{"w":"coarse","p":"adj.","d":"rough and not fine or smooth","c":"粗糙的；粗的","s":"The flour from the old stone mill is coarse, but the bread has a rich taste, so tourists queue to buy it.","t":"老石磨磨出的麵粉很粗，但做出的麵包風味濃郁，所以遊客都排隊購買。"}]},{"unit":9,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 2 (collateral – embargo)","cards":[{"w":"collateral","p":"adj.","d":"happening as an extra, unplanned result of something","c":"附帶的；間接的","s":"The chemicals killed the insects, but there was collateral damage to the bees, and the fruit trees produced less fruit.","t":"化學藥劑殺死了害蟲，但也對蜜蜂造成附帶傷害，而果樹的結果量也減少了。"},{"w":"compatibility","p":"n.","d":"the ability to exist or work together without problems","c":"相容性","s":"The farmer tested the compatibility of the two plants, because some crops grow badly when they are planted side by side.","t":"農夫測試了兩種植物的相容性，因為有些作物並排種植時會長得不好。"},{"w":"complementary","p":"adj.","d":"adding something useful so that two things work well together","c":"互補的","s":"Rice and beans have complementary proteins, so eating them together gives the body what it needs.","t":"米和豆類的蛋白質是互補的，所以一起吃能提供身體所需的營養。"},{"w":"composite","p":"adj.","d":"made of several different parts or materials","c":"合成的；綜合的","s":"The report used a composite score based on price, safety and taste, and the local brand came first.","t":"這份報告採用以價格、安全和口味為基礎的綜合分數，而本地品牌拿下第一名。"},{"w":"concoct","p":"v.","d":"to make something by mixing different things, often in a new way","c":"調製；調配","s":"The chef likes to concoct new sauces from local fruit, and his mango chilli dip has become very popular.","t":"這位主廚喜歡用本地水果調製新醬料，而他的芒果辣椒沾醬已經大受歡迎。"},{"w":"confound","p":"v.","d":"to confuse or surprise someone because it is unexpected","c":"使困惑；使驚訝","s":"The tiny farm's huge harvest confound the experts, because it used no chemicals at all.","t":"這座小農場的大豐收讓專家們大感困惑，因為它完全沒有使用任何化學藥劑。"},{"w":"connoisseur","p":"n.","d":"an expert who knows a lot about food, drink or art","c":"鑑賞家；行家","s":"My uncle is a tea connoisseur, and he can tell which mountain a tea comes from just by smelling it.","t":"我叔叔是茶葉行家，而且他光聞味道就能說出茶來自哪座山。"},{"w":"consignment","p":"n.","d":"a quantity of goods sent to someone","c":"一批貨物","s":"A consignment of mangoes was stopped at the border, because officials found insects inside some of the boxes.","t":"一批芒果在邊境被攔下，因為官員在部分箱子裡發現了昆蟲。"},{"w":"contaminant","p":"n.","d":"a substance that makes something dirty or unsafe","c":"污染物","s":"The lab found a dangerous contaminant in the river water, so farmers were told not to use it for their crops.","t":"實驗室在河水中發現了一種危險的污染物，所以農民被告知不要用它灌溉作物。"},{"w":"contrive","p":"v.","d":"to manage to do something difficult, often by being clever","c":"設法做到","s":"The family contrive to feed six children on a very small income, and the mother grew most of their vegetables herself.","t":"這家人以很微薄的收入設法養活了六個孩子，而母親自己種了大部分的蔬菜。"},{"w":"corollary","p":"n.","d":"a natural result of something else","c":"必然結果","s":"Cheaper food is one corollary of modern farming, but another is the loss of many small family farms.","t":"更便宜的食物是現代農業的一個必然結果，但另一個結果則是許多小型家庭農場的消失。"},{"w":"counterfeit","p":"adj.","d":"made to look real in order to trick people","c":"偽造的；仿冒的","s":"Police seized thousands of bottles of counterfeit wine, and the labels looked so real that shops had no idea.","t":"警方查獲了數千瓶仿冒葡萄酒，而標籤看起來太逼真，連商店都毫不知情。"},{"w":"debase","p":"v.","d":"to reduce the quality or value of something","c":"降低（品質或價值）","s":"Adding cheap oil would debase the quality of the olive oil, so the brand checks every batch carefully.","t":"添加便宜的油會降低橄欖油的品質，所以這個品牌仔細檢查每一批產品。"},{"w":"deflate","p":"v.","d":"to make someone lose confidence or hope","c":"使洩氣","s":"The terrible harvest deflate the young farmer, but his neighbours encouraged him to try again the next year.","t":"糟糕的收成讓這位年輕農夫很洩氣，但鄰居們鼓勵他明年再試一次。"},{"w":"delicacy","p":"n.","d":"a rare or expensive food that is special to eat","c":"佳餚；珍饈","s":"Mullet roe is a delicacy in Taiwan, so families often give it as a gift during Lunar New Year.","t":"烏魚子在台灣是一種珍饈，所以家家戶戶常在農曆新年時把它當作禮物送人。"},{"w":"depletion","p":"n.","d":"the reduction of something until little is left","c":"耗盡；枯竭","s":"The depletion of groundwater is a serious issue in the south, and some land has sunk below sea level.","t":"地下水枯竭是南部嚴重的問題，而有些土地已經下陷到海平面以下。"},{"w":"deposit","p":"n.","d":"a layer of something left by water or natural processes","c":"沉積物；沉積層","s":"The river leaves a rich deposit of mud after each flood, so the farmland along its banks is very fertile.","t":"每次洪水過後河流都會留下一層肥沃的泥沉積物，所以沿岸的農地非常肥沃。"},{"w":"deregulation","p":"n.","d":"the removal of government rules from an industry","c":"解除管制；鬆綁","s":"The deregulation of rice prices helped some farmers earn more, but others struggled because big companies paid them less.","t":"米價鬆綁讓部分農民賺得更多，但其他人卻過得很辛苦，因為大公司付給他們的錢更少了。"},{"w":"devour","p":"v.","d":"to eat something quickly and hungrily","c":"狼吞虎嚥；吞食","s":"The hungry caterpillars devour the cabbage leaves overnight, so the farmer found only holes in the morning.","t":"飢餓的毛毛蟲一夜之間吞食了高麗菜葉，所以農夫早上只看到滿是破洞。"},{"w":"discerning","p":"adj.","d":"able to judge the quality of something well","c":"有眼光的；有辨別力的","s":"discerning shoppers check where their vegetables come from, and they are willing to pay more for local produce.","t":"有眼光的消費者會查看蔬菜的產地，而且他們願意為本地農產品多付錢。"},{"w":"disincentive","p":"n.","d":"something that makes people less willing to do something","c":"抑制因素；阻礙","s":"Low prices are a disincentive for young farmers, so few of them want to grow rice like their grandparents did.","t":"低價是年輕農民的阻礙，所以他們之中很少人想像祖父母那樣種稻。"},{"w":"dosage","p":"n.","d":"the amount of a medicine or chemical given at one time","c":"劑量","s":"The vet checked the dosage carefully before treating the cows, because too much medicine could end up in the milk.","t":"獸醫在治療乳牛前仔細確認劑量，因為過多的藥物可能會殘留在牛奶裡。"},{"w":"ebb","p":"v.","d":"to slowly become less or weaker","c":"衰退；減弱","s":"Interest in the new diet began to ebb after a few months, and the shop stopped selling the special products.","t":"對這種新飲食法的興趣在幾個月後開始減退，而商店也停止販售那些特殊產品。"},{"w":"elasticity","p":"n.","d":"how much demand changes when prices change","c":"彈性","s":"Rice has low price elasticity, so people still buy it when it becomes more expensive, but they cut back on snacks.","t":"米的價格彈性很低，所以即使變貴了人們仍會購買，但他們會減少吃零食。"},{"w":"embargo","p":"n.","d":"an official ban on trade with another country","c":"禁運","s":"The embargo on pork exports hurt farmers badly, so the government gave them money to survive.","t":"豬肉出口禁運嚴重打擊了農民，所以政府發放補助金讓他們度過難關。"}]},{"unit":10,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 3 (extraneous – irreparable)","cards":[{"w":"extraneous","p":"adj.","d":"not connected to the main subject; unnecessary","c":"無關的；外來的","s":"The recipe contains no extraneous ingredients, and it uses only rice, water and a little salt.","t":"這份食譜不含任何多餘的食材，而且只用米、水和一點點鹽。"},{"w":"fathom","p":"v.","d":"to understand something difficult","c":"理解；看透","s":"Many city children cannot fathom how much work goes into growing rice, so the school takes them to a farm every year.","t":"許多城市孩子無法理解種稻需要付出多少勞力，所以學校每年都帶他們去農場。"},{"w":"fluctuation","p":"n.","d":"a change up and down in amount or level","c":"波動","s":"The fluctuation in vegetable prices is huge in Taiwan, because one typhoon can destroy crops across the whole island.","t":"台灣菜價的波動很大，因為一個颱風就能摧毀全島的作物。"},{"w":"fortuitous","p":"adj.","d":"happening by lucky chance","c":"幸運的；偶然的","s":"The discovery of the new tea flavour was fortuitous, because insects bit the leaves and changed their taste.","t":"這種新茶風味的發現是偶然的，因為昆蟲咬了葉子而改變了它們的味道。"},{"w":"fruition","p":"n.","d":"the point at which a plan becomes real","c":"實現；成果","s":"Her dream of opening a farm cafe finally came to fruition last year, and it is now full of visitors every weekend.","t":"她開農場咖啡館的夢想終於在去年實現，而現在每個週末都擠滿了遊客。"},{"w":"glut","p":"n.","d":"too much of something, more than is needed","c":"過剩；供過於求","s":"There was a glut of cabbages this winter, so prices fell sharply and some farmers left them to rot in the field.","t":"今年冬天高麗菜供過於求，所以價格暴跌，有些農民乾脆讓它們爛在田裡。"},{"w":"gratify","p":"v.","d":"to please someone or satisfy a desire","c":"使滿足；使高興","s":"It gratify the farmers to see children enjoying their fruit, and they invited the class to visit again next year.","t":"看到孩子們享用他們的水果讓農民們很欣慰，而且他們邀請這個班級明年再來參觀。"},{"w":"hardy","p":"adj.","d":"strong and able to survive difficult conditions","c":"耐寒的；耐勞的","s":"Sweet potatoes are hardy plants, so they can grow in poor soil where rice would never survive.","t":"地瓜是生命力強的植物，所以它們能在稻米絕對無法存活的貧瘠土壤中生長。"},{"w":"haul","p":"n.","d":"an amount of something that has been caught or taken","c":"捕獲量；收穫","s":"The fishermen came back with a huge haul of squid, so the harbour market was busy all night.","t":"漁夫們帶回了大量的魷魚漁獲，所以港口市場整晚都很熱鬧。"},{"w":"hefty","p":"adj.","d":"large in amount, especially money","c":"高額的；大量的","s":"The restaurant received a hefty fine for using expired meat, and it lost many customers after the news spread.","t":"這家餐廳因使用過期肉品而被處以高額罰款，而且消息傳開後失去了許多顧客。"},{"w":"imperceptible","p":"adj.","d":"too small to be noticed","c":"察覺不到的；極細微的","s":"The change in taste was almost imperceptible, but the company had cut the sugar by twenty percent.","t":"口味的改變幾乎察覺不到，但公司已經把糖減少了百分之二十。"},{"w":"impervious","p":"adj.","d":"not affected by something, or not letting water through","c":"不受影響的；不透水的","s":"The new rice seems impervious to the disease, so farmers who planted it saved their whole harvest.","t":"這種新稻米似乎不受這種病害影響，所以種植它的農民保住了整季的收成。"},{"w":"implausible","p":"adj.","d":"difficult to believe","c":"難以置信的","s":"The advert's claim that the tea can cure every illness is implausible, so the government ordered the company to remove it.","t":"廣告宣稱這款茶能治百病的說法令人難以置信，所以政府命令公司撤下廣告。"},{"w":"incidental","p":"adj.","d":"happening as a minor part of something else","c":"附帶的；次要的","s":"Saving money was only an incidental benefit, because the main reason she grew vegetables was to relax after work.","t":"省錢只是附帶的好處，因為她種菜的主要原因是下班後放鬆。"},{"w":"incompatible","p":"adj.","d":"not able to exist or work together","c":"不相容的；互相抵觸的","s":"Cheap food and fair wages for farmers can seem incompatible, but fair trade shows that both are possible.","t":"便宜的食物與農民的合理工資看似互相抵觸，但公平貿易證明兩者可以兼得。"},{"w":"inconclusive","p":"adj.","d":"not giving a clear result","c":"無定論的；不確定的","s":"The study on coffee and health was inconclusive, so scientists plan to follow more people for a longer time.","t":"這項咖啡與健康的研究沒有定論，所以科學家計畫追蹤更多人更長的時間。"},{"w":"indulge","p":"v.","d":"to allow yourself to enjoy something special","c":"沉溺；放縱享受","s":"I indulge in a big slice of cake after my exams, but I usually try to avoid sweet food.","t":"考完試後我會放縱自己吃一大塊蛋糕，但平常我盡量避免吃甜食。"},{"w":"inedible","p":"adj.","d":"not fit or safe to eat","c":"不能吃的","s":"Some wild mushrooms look delicious but are inedible, so you should never pick them unless an expert is with you.","t":"有些野生菇類看起來很美味，卻是不能吃的，所以除非有專家同行，否則你絕不該採摘。"},{"w":"inert","p":"adj.","d":"not producing a chemical reaction","c":"惰性的；無作用的","s":"The gas used in the snack bags is inert, so it keeps the chips fresh and does not change their taste.","t":"零食袋裡使用的氣體是惰性的，所以它能保持洋芋片新鮮，又不會改變味道。"},{"w":"infusion","p":"n.","d":"a drink made by soaking leaves or fruit in hot water; or adding something new","c":"浸泡液；注入","s":"The government's infusion of money into agritech has attracted young people, and several new start-ups have opened.","t":"政府對農業科技的資金注入吸引了年輕人，而且已經有好幾家新創公司成立。"},{"w":"innumerable","p":"adj.","d":"too many to be counted","c":"無數的","s":"There are innumerable ways to cook tofu, so my grandmother never serves it the same way twice in a week.","t":"豆腐有無數種料理方式，所以我奶奶一週內從不用同一種方式煮它。"},{"w":"insolvent","p":"adj.","d":"unable to pay debts","c":"無力償債的；破產的","s":"Several pig farms became insolvent after the disease outbreak, and the owners had to sell their land.","t":"疫情爆發後，好幾座養豬場無力償債，而場主們只好賣掉土地。"},{"w":"instantaneous","p":"adj.","d":"happening immediately","c":"瞬間的；即時的","s":"The effect of the new app was almost instantaneous, because farmers could suddenly sell directly to customers.","t":"這款新應用程式的效果幾乎是立竿見影的，因為農民突然間就能直接賣給顧客。"},{"w":"intake","p":"n.","d":"the amount of food or drink you take into your body","c":"攝取量","s":"Doctors advise teenagers to reduce their sugar intake, because too much can harm their teeth and health.","t":"醫生建議青少年減少糖的攝取量，因為攝取過多會傷害牙齒和健康。"},{"w":"irreparable","p":"adj.","d":"too bad to be repaired or put right","c":"無法挽回的；不可修復的","s":"The chemical spill caused irreparable damage to the farmland, so the owners could never grow crops there again.","t":"化學物質外洩對農地造成無法挽回的損害，所以地主再也無法在那裡種植作物。"}]},{"unit":11,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 4 (judicious – profusion)","cards":[{"w":"judicious","p":"adj.","d":"showing good judgement","c":"明智的；審慎的","s":"With judicious use of water, the farm survived the drought, while neighbouring farms lost most of their crops.","t":"透過審慎的用水，這座農場撐過了乾旱，而鄰近的農場卻損失了大部分的作物。"},{"w":"leniency","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being less strict than expected","c":"寬大；從輕","s":"The court showed no leniency to the company that sold fake oil, and the owner was sent to prison.","t":"法院對販售假油的公司毫不寬貸，而老闆被送進了監獄。"},{"w":"misguided","p":"adj.","d":"based on wrong ideas or judgement","c":"被誤導的；錯誤的","s":"The idea that all fat is bad is misguided, because our bodies need healthy fats from fish and nuts.","t":"所有脂肪都不好的觀念是錯誤的，因為我們的身體需要從魚和堅果中攝取健康的脂肪。"},{"w":"mismanagement","p":"n.","d":"bad or careless control of something","c":"管理不當","s":"The water shortage was caused partly by mismanagement, because old pipes leaked and nobody repaired them.","t":"缺水的部分原因是管理不當，因為老舊的水管漏水卻沒有人修理。"},{"w":"nourish","p":"v.","d":"to give a living thing the food it needs to grow","c":"滋養；養育","s":"Breast milk nourish babies in their first months, and it also protects them from many diseases.","t":"母乳在嬰兒出生後的頭幾個月滋養他們，而且也保護他們免於許多疾病。"},{"w":"nourishment","p":"n.","d":"food needed to live and grow","c":"營養；食物","s":"The plants get nourishment from the fish waste in the water, so the farmer does not need to add fertiliser.","t":"植物從水中的魚排泄物獲得養分，所以農夫不需要添加肥料。"},{"w":"noxious","p":"adj.","d":"harmful or poisonous","c":"有毒的；有害的","s":"The factory released noxious gases near the farms, and the farmers noticed brown spots on their vegetables.","t":"工廠在農場附近排放了有毒氣體，而農民注意到他們的蔬菜上出現了褐色斑點。"},{"w":"obsolescence","p":"n.","d":"the state of becoming old-fashioned and no longer used","c":"過時；淘汰","s":"Hand tools are heading towards obsolescence on large farms, but many small farmers in the mountains still use them every day.","t":"在大型農場上手工具正逐漸走向淘汰，但山區許多小農仍然每天使用它們。"},{"w":"offshoot","p":"n.","d":"something that develops from something larger","c":"分支；衍生物","s":"The farm cafe began as an offshoot of the family's fruit business, but now it earns more money than the orchard.","t":"這間農場咖啡館起初只是家族水果事業的分支，但現在它賺的錢比果園還多。"},{"w":"opportune","p":"adj.","d":"happening at a suitable time","c":"適時的；恰好的","s":"The rain came at an opportune moment, because the rice plants needed water just as the dry season was starting.","t":"雨來得正是時候，因為乾季剛開始時稻子正需要水。"},{"w":"overabundance","p":"n.","d":"too large an amount of something","c":"過多；過剩","s":"An overabundance of choice in supermarkets can confuse shoppers, so some stores now offer fewer brands.","t":"超市選擇過多可能會讓消費者困惑，所以有些商店現在提供較少的品牌。"},{"w":"overconsumption","p":"n.","d":"using or eating too much of something","c":"過度消費；過量攝取","s":"The overconsumption of meat in rich countries puts pressure on land and water, so experts suggest eating more beans.","t":"富裕國家對肉類的過度消費對土地和水資源造成壓力，所以專家建議多吃豆類。"},{"w":"overproduction","p":"n.","d":"producing more of something than people need","c":"生產過剩","s":"overproduction of milk caused prices to fall, so some farmers poured it away because they could not sell it.","t":"牛奶生產過剩導致價格下跌，所以有些農民因為賣不出去而把牛奶倒掉。"},{"w":"overstate","p":"v.","d":"to describe something as bigger or more important than it really is","c":"誇大","s":"Food companies sometimes overstate the health benefits of their products, so you should read the label carefully.","t":"食品公司有時會誇大產品的健康益處，所以你應該仔細閱讀標籤。"},{"w":"palatable","p":"adj.","d":"pleasant enough to eat, or acceptable","c":"可口的；可接受的","s":"The chef added herbs to make the vegetables more palatable, and the children finally finished their plates.","t":"主廚加了香草讓蔬菜更可口，而孩子們終於把盤子裡的東西吃完了。"},{"w":"pernicious","p":"adj.","d":"having a harmful effect, especially slowly and secretly","c":"有害的；惡性的","s":"Sugary drinks have a pernicious effect on children's teeth, so the school has stopped selling them.","t":"含糖飲料對兒童牙齒有有害的影響，所以學校已經停止販售。"},{"w":"pertain","p":"v.","d":"to be connected with a particular subject","c":"與……有關","s":"These rules pertain to all restaurants in the city, so even small noodle stalls must follow them.","t":"這些規定適用於市內所有餐廳，所以即使是小麵攤也必須遵守。"},{"w":"potency","p":"n.","d":"the strength of something, such as a drug or chemical","c":"效力；強度","s":"The potency of the pesticide was so high that it killed helpful insects too, so the farmer switched to a gentler product.","t":"這種農藥的效力太強，連益蟲也一起殺死了，所以農夫改用較溫和的產品。"},{"w":"precipitous","p":"adj.","d":"sudden and very large (of a fall)","c":"急遽的；陡峭的","s":"There was a precipitous drop in banana prices last month, and many farmers lost money on every box they sold.","t":"上個月香蕉價格急遽下跌，而許多農民每賣一箱都在賠錢。"},{"w":"predatory","p":"adj.","d":"trying to take advantage of weaker people","c":"掠奪性的；剝削的","s":"Some lenders use predatory practices with poor farmers, so the government offers low-interest loans instead.","t":"有些放款人對貧窮農民採取掠奪性的手段，所以政府改為提供低利貸款。"},{"w":"preponderance","p":"n.","d":"a larger number or amount of one kind than others","c":"多數；優勢","s":"There is a preponderance of elderly workers on Taiwan's farms, so experts worry about who will grow food in the future.","t":"台灣的農場上以年長工作者居多，所以專家擔心未來由誰來種植糧食。"},{"w":"prevalent","p":"adj.","d":"common or widespread at a particular time","c":"普遍的；盛行的","s":"Eating breakfast outside is prevalent in Taiwan, and there is a breakfast shop on almost every street corner.","t":"在台灣外食早餐很普遍，而且幾乎每個街角都有一家早餐店。"},{"w":"procurement","p":"n.","d":"the process of buying supplies for an organisation","c":"採購","s":"The school changed its procurement rules, so it now buys rice and vegetables directly from farms in the county.","t":"學校修改了採購規定，所以現在直接向縣內的農場購買米和蔬菜。"},{"w":"prodigious","p":"adj.","d":"very large or impressive","c":"巨大的；驚人的","s":"The festival needs a prodigious amount of rice, so the organisers order it from several farms months in advance.","t":"這個節慶需要驚人的米量，所以主辦單位提前好幾個月向多座農場訂購。"},{"w":"profusion","p":"n.","d":"a very large amount of something","c":"大量；豐富","s":"In spring the orchard is a profusion of white flowers, and bees come from miles around to visit them.","t":"春天時果園開滿大量白花，而蜜蜂從好幾哩外飛來拜訪它們。"}]},{"unit":12,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 5 (prohibitive – succulent)","cards":[{"w":"prohibitive","p":"adj.","d":"so expensive that people cannot afford it","c":"高昂得令人卻步的","s":"The cost of a vertical farm is prohibitive for most small farmers, so only large companies can build one.","t":"垂直農場的成本對大多數小農來說高得令人卻步，所以只有大公司蓋得起。"},{"w":"prominence","p":"n.","d":"the state of being important or well known","c":"顯著；重要地位","s":"Plant-based food has gained prominence in recent years, and even fast-food chains now offer vegetarian burgers.","t":"近年來植物性食品逐漸取得重要地位，而且連速食連鎖店現在都提供素食漢堡。"},{"w":"proprietary","p":"adj.","d":"owned by a company and protected by law","c":"專利的；專有的","s":"The company keeps its sauce recipe proprietary, so only three people in the factory know all the ingredients.","t":"這家公司把醬料配方列為專有機密，所以工廠裡只有三個人知道全部的成分。"},{"w":"prudence","p":"n.","d":"careful and sensible judgement","c":"審慎；謹慎","s":"Farmers show prudence by saving part of their seeds every year, so they can replant if a typhoon destroys the crop.","t":"農民每年保留一部分種子，展現了他們的審慎，這樣如果颱風摧毀作物，他們就能重新播種。"},{"w":"reallocate","p":"v.","d":"to give something to a different person or purpose","c":"重新分配","s":"The government decided to reallocate water from factories to farms during the drought, but factory owners were unhappy.","t":"政府決定在乾旱期間把工廠的用水重新分配給農場，但工廠老闆們很不高興。"},{"w":"reciprocity","p":"n.","d":"exchanging things with others for mutual benefit","c":"互惠","s":"Village life was based on reciprocity, because neighbours helped each other at harvest time and shared food.","t":"鄉村生活建立在互惠的基礎上，因為鄰居們在收成時互相幫忙並分享食物。"},{"w":"recuperate","p":"v.","d":"to recover after an illness or a difficult time","c":"恢復；復原","s":"The land needs a few years to recuperate after the flood, so the farmers are growing grass there for now.","t":"洪水過後，這塊土地需要幾年時間來恢復，所以農民目前在那裡種草。"},{"w":"redistribute","p":"v.","d":"to share something out again in a different way","c":"重新分配","s":"The app helps shops redistribute unsold food to charities, so less bread and fruit end up in the bin.","t":"這款應用程式幫助商店把沒賣完的食物重新分配給慈善機構，所以較少的麵包和水果最後被丟進垃圾桶。"},{"w":"regress","p":"v.","d":"to go back to an earlier, worse state","c":"倒退；退步","s":"Without new young farmers, the village's farming could regress, and old fields could turn back into forest.","t":"如果沒有新的年輕農民，村裡的農業可能會倒退，而老田也可能重新變回森林。"},{"w":"reliance","p":"n.","d":"the state of depending on something","c":"依賴","s":"Taiwan's reliance on imported wheat worries some experts, because a global crisis could suddenly cut supplies.","t":"台灣對進口小麥的依賴讓一些專家擔憂，因為全球危機可能突然切斷供應。"},{"w":"residual","p":"adj.","d":"remaining after most of something has gone","c":"殘留的","s":"The lab found residual pesticide on the vegetables, so the farmer was told to wait longer before harvesting.","t":"實驗室在蔬菜上發現殘留的農藥，所以農夫被告知要等更久才能採收。"},{"w":"satiate","p":"v.","d":"to satisfy hunger completely","c":"使飽足；使滿足","s":"A bowl of beef noodle soup can satiate even a very hungry student, and it costs less than a fast-food meal.","t":"一碗牛肉麵就能讓即使非常餓的學生吃飽，而且比一份速食餐還便宜。"},{"w":"savour","p":"v.","d":"to enjoy the taste of food slowly","c":"細細品嚐","s":"My grandfather likes to savour his tea slowly, and he says that people today eat and drink far too quickly.","t":"我爺爺喜歡慢慢地品味他的茶，而且他說現在的人吃喝都太快了。"},{"w":"scourge","p":"n.","d":"something that causes great trouble or suffering","c":"禍害；災難","s":"Locusts have been a scourge for farmers for thousands of years, and swarms still destroy crops in parts of Africa.","t":"數千年來蝗蟲一直是農民的禍害，而在非洲部分地區，蝗群至今仍在摧毀作物。"},{"w":"seasonality","p":"n.","d":"the way something changes with the seasons","c":"季節性","s":"The seasonality of fruit means that mangoes are cheap in summer, but you can hardly find them in winter.","t":"水果的季節性意味著芒果在夏天很便宜，但冬天幾乎買不到。"},{"w":"self-sufficiency","p":"n.","d":"the ability to produce everything you need yourself","c":"自給自足","s":"Taiwan's food self-sufficiency rate is only about thirty percent, so the country imports most of its grain.","t":"台灣的糧食自給率只有大約百分之三十，所以國家大部分的穀物都仰賴進口。"},{"w":"sequester","p":"v.","d":"to store or capture something, such as carbon, so it is kept away","c":"封存；隔離","s":"Healthy soil can sequester carbon from the air, so better farming could help fight climate change.","t":"健康的土壤能封存空氣中的碳，所以更好的耕作方式有助於對抗氣候變遷。"},{"w":"shrewd","p":"adj.","d":"clever at understanding situations and making good decisions","c":"精明的","s":"The shrewd farmer sold his crop before the price fell, and his neighbours wished they had done the same.","t":"這位精明的農夫在價格下跌前就賣掉了作物，而他的鄰居們都希望自己也這麼做了。"},{"w":"smother","p":"v.","d":"to cover something completely so it cannot breathe or grow","c":"覆蓋；悶死","s":"Thick weeds can smother young plants, so farmers remove them before the seedlings lose their sunlight.","t":"茂密的雜草會悶死幼小的植物，所以農民會在幼苗失去陽光前把它們清除。"},{"w":"sourcing","p":"n.","d":"the process of finding where to get supplies","c":"採購來源；貨源管理","s":"The restaurant is proud of its local sourcing, and every vegetable comes from farms less than fifty kilometres away.","t":"這家餐廳以在地採購為傲，而且每一種蔬菜都來自五十公里內的農場。"},{"w":"sparingly","p":"adv.","d":"in small amounts; not much","c":"節省地；少量地","s":"Use salt sparingly when you cook for elderly people, because too much can raise their blood pressure.","t":"為長者烹調時要少量使用鹽，因為太多可能會讓他們的血壓升高。"},{"w":"stagnation","p":"n.","d":"a state of no growth or change","c":"停滯","s":"Farm incomes have been in stagnation for years, so many young people choose office jobs in the city.","t":"農業收入多年來一直處於停滯，所以許多年輕人選擇到城市從事辦公室工作。"},{"w":"subsist","p":"v.","d":"to manage to stay alive with very little food or money","c":"勉強維生","s":"During the war, families had to subsist on sweet potatoes, and rice was a luxury for special days.","t":"戰爭期間，家家戶戶只能靠地瓜勉強維生，而白米是特殊日子才吃得到的奢侈品。"},{"w":"substantive","p":"adj.","d":"real, important and serious","c":"實質的；重大的","s":"The new law brought substantive changes to food labels, so shoppers can now see clearly where ingredients come from.","t":"新法為食品標示帶來了實質的改變，所以消費者現在能清楚看到成分的來源。"},{"w":"succulent","p":"adj.","d":"juicy and delicious","c":"多汁的","s":"The pineapples from Pingtung are sweet and succulent, so they are sent as gifts to friends overseas.","t":"屏東的鳳梨又甜又多汁，所以人們把它們當作禮物寄給海外的朋友。"}]},{"unit":13,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 6 (suffice – auxiliary)","cards":[{"w":"suffice","p":"v.","d":"to be enough","c":"足夠","s":"A small fridge will suffice for one person, but a family of five needs a much larger one.","t":"小冰箱對一個人來說就足夠了，但五口之家需要大得多的冰箱。"},{"w":"susceptibility","p":"n.","d":"how easily something is affected or harmed","c":"易感性；敏感度","s":"Bananas have a high susceptibility to disease, because almost all of them are genetically identical.","t":"香蕉對病害的易感性很高，因為它們幾乎全都基因相同。"},{"w":"sustenance","p":"n.","d":"food and drink that keeps someone alive","c":"食物；營養來源","s":"For many poor families, rice is the main source of sustenance, so a rise in its price can cause real hunger.","t":"對許多貧困家庭來說，米是主要的糧食來源，所以它的價格上漲可能會造成真正的飢餓。"},{"w":"symptomatic","p":"adj.","d":"showing that a bigger problem exists","c":"有代表性的；徵兆性的","s":"Empty fields are symptomatic of a deeper problem, because young people do not see a future in farming.","t":"荒廢的田地反映出更深層的問題，因為年輕人看不到務農的未來。"},{"w":"tamper","p":"v.","d":"to change something without permission, often to cause harm","c":"竄改；亂動","s":"Someone tried to tamper with the labels on the milk cartons, so the shop removed them all from the shelves.","t":"有人企圖竄改牛奶盒上的標籤，所以商店把它們全部從架上撤下。"},{"w":"tantamount","p":"adj.","d":"equal in effect to something worse","c":"等同於","s":"Selling expired meat to families is tantamount to poisoning customers on purpose, so the punishment is very serious.","t":"把過期肉品賣給家庭等同於故意毒害顧客，所以懲罰非常嚴厲。"},{"w":"tenable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be defended or kept going","c":"站得住腳的；可維持的","s":"Growing rice on such dry land is no longer tenable, so the farmers are switching to crops that need less water.","t":"在這麼乾燥的土地上種稻已經無法維持了，所以農民正改種需水量較少的作物。"},{"w":"tolerable","p":"adj.","d":"acceptable, though not very good","c":"尚可的；可忍受的","s":"The food at the camp was tolerable, but everyone was so hungry after hiking that nobody complained.","t":"營地的食物還過得去，但健行後大家都餓壞了，所以沒有人抱怨。"},{"w":"toxicity","p":"n.","d":"how poisonous something is","c":"毒性","s":"Scientists measured the toxicity of the new pesticide, and they found it was too dangerous for fish in nearby rivers.","t":"科學家測量了新農藥的毒性，而他們發現它對附近河流中的魚類太危險了。"},{"w":"traceability","p":"n.","d":"the ability to follow where a product came from","c":"可追溯性；產銷履歷","s":"The QR code improves traceability, so customers can see which farm grew their rice and when it was harvested.","t":"這個QR碼提升了可追溯性，所以顧客能看到哪座農場種了他們的米，以及何時收割。"},{"w":"unfettered","p":"adj.","d":"not limited by rules","c":"不受限制的","s":"unfettered use of chemicals damaged the land for decades, so stricter rules were finally introduced.","t":"不受限制地使用化學藥劑破壞了土地數十年，所以終於訂定了更嚴格的規定。"},{"w":"unsustainable","p":"adj.","d":"not able to continue at the same level","c":"不可持續的","s":"Pumping so much groundwater is unsustainable, because the land is sinking and the wells are drying up.","t":"抽取這麼多地下水是不可持續的，因為土地正在下陷，水井也在乾涸。"},{"w":"upsurge","p":"n.","d":"a sudden increase","c":"激增","s":"There has been an upsurge in home gardening since the pandemic, and seed shops have sold out of many vegetables.","t":"疫情以來居家園藝出現了激增，而種子店的許多蔬菜種子都已經賣光了。"},{"w":"vanguard","p":"n.","d":"the leading position in developing new ideas","c":"先鋒；前衛","s":"The Netherlands is in the vanguard of greenhouse farming, so experts from many countries go there to learn.","t":"荷蘭處於溫室農業的先鋒地位，所以許多國家的專家都去那裡學習。"},{"w":"verifiable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be checked and proved true","c":"可驗證的","s":"The organic label must be based on verifiable tests, so inspectors visit farms and take soil samples.","t":"有機標章必須以可驗證的檢測為依據，所以稽查員會造訪農場並採集土壤樣本。"},{"w":"viability","p":"n.","d":"the ability to work successfully","c":"可行性；生存能力","s":"The bank questioned the viability of the indoor farm, because electricity costs were so high.","t":"銀行質疑這座室內農場的可行性，因為電費實在太高了。"},{"w":"voracious","p":"adj.","d":"eating or wanting a very large amount","c":"貪吃的；狼吞虎嚥的","s":"Teenage boys often have voracious appetites, so their parents are surprised by how much rice they eat.","t":"青春期男孩常常食量驚人，所以他們的父母對他們吃那麼多飯感到驚訝。"},{"w":"vulnerability","p":"n.","d":"the state of being easily hurt or damaged","c":"脆弱性","s":"The typhoon showed the vulnerability of the island's food supply, because vegetable prices doubled within days.","t":"颱風顯示出這座島嶼糧食供應的脆弱性，因為蔬菜價格在幾天內就翻倍了。"},{"w":"wean","p":"v.","d":"to make someone stop depending on something","c":"使戒除；使逐漸擺脫","s":"The campaign tries to wean students off sugary drinks, so the school offers free cold water instead.","t":"這項運動試圖讓學生戒掉含糖飲料，所以學校改為提供免費的冰開水。"},{"w":"withhold","p":"v.","d":"to refuse to give something","c":"扣留；拒絕給予","s":"The supermarket withheld payment from the farm, because the vegetables arrived late and many were damaged.","t":"超市扣留了對農場的付款，因為蔬菜送達得太晚，而且許多都已損壞。"},{"w":"zeal","p":"n.","d":"great energy and enthusiasm","c":"熱忱；熱情","s":"The young farmers worked with great zeal, and they turned the empty fields into a thriving organic farm.","t":"年輕農民們滿懷熱忱地工作，並把空地變成了一座欣欣向榮的有機農場。"},{"w":"adjunct","p":"n.","d":"something added to a more important thing","c":"附屬物；輔助","s":"Vitamin pills should only be an adjunct to a healthy diet, so doctors say you cannot live on pills alone.","t":"維他命丸只應該作為健康飲食的輔助，所以醫生說你不能只靠藥丸過活。"},{"w":"ancillary","p":"adj.","d":"providing extra help or support","c":"輔助的；附屬的","s":"The farm earns ancillary income from school visits, and this money helps when the harvest is poor.","t":"這座農場從學校參訪中獲得附加收入，而這筆錢在收成不佳時很有幫助。"},{"w":"attenuate","p":"v.","d":"to make something weaker or less strong","c":"減弱；削弱","s":"Trees planted around the fields can attenuate strong winds, so the crops are less likely to be damaged.","t":"在田地周圍種樹可以減弱強風，所以作物比較不容易受損。"},{"w":"auxiliary","p":"adj.","d":"giving extra help or support","c":"輔助的；備用的","s":"The farm installed an auxiliary generator, so the fridges keep working even when a typhoon cuts the power.","t":"這座農場安裝了一台備用發電機，所以即使颱風造成停電，冰箱也能繼續運作。"}]},{"unit":14,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 7 (bedrock – inequitable)","cards":[{"w":"bedrock","p":"n.","d":"the basic idea or thing on which others are built","c":"基礎；根本","s":"Trust is the bedrock of the food business, so one safety scandal can ruin a famous brand.","t":"信任是食品業的根本，所以一起食安醜聞就能毀掉一個知名品牌。"},{"w":"counterbalance","p":"v.","d":"to have an equal but opposite effect on something","c":"抵銷；平衡","s":"Higher prices for organic food counterbalance the smaller harvests, so organic farmers can still earn a living.","t":"有機食品較高的價格抵銷了較少的收成，所以有機農民仍能維持生計。"},{"w":"counterintuitive","p":"adj.","d":"the opposite of what you would expect","c":"違反直覺的","s":"It seems counterintuitive, but leaving some weeds in the field can actually help crops, because they attract useful insects.","t":"這似乎違反直覺，但在田裡留一些雜草其實對作物有幫助，因為它們能吸引益蟲。"},{"w":"cyclical","p":"adj.","d":"happening in a repeated pattern","c":"週期性的","s":"Pig prices are cyclical, so they rise for a few years and then fall when too many farmers start raising pigs.","t":"豬價是週期性的，所以它們會上漲幾年，然後在太多農民開始養豬時下跌。"},{"w":"deceptive","p":"adj.","d":"making you believe something false","c":"誤導的；欺騙的","s":"The packaging is deceptive, because the box is large but there are only a few cookies inside.","t":"這個包裝很誤導人，因為盒子很大，裡面卻只有幾片餅乾。"},{"w":"discretionary","p":"adj.","d":"decided by a person's own choice","c":"可自由支配的","s":"Families spend less on discretionary items like snacks when food prices rise, but they still buy rice and eggs.","t":"當食物價格上漲時，家庭會減少在零食等非必需品上的花費，但他們仍然會買米和蛋。"},{"w":"divisive","p":"adj.","d":"causing strong disagreement between people","c":"造成分歧的","s":"The import of American pork was a divisive issue in Taiwan, and people argued about it for months.","t":"進口美國豬肉在台灣是個引發分歧的議題，而人們為此爭論了好幾個月。"},{"w":"egregious","p":"adj.","d":"extremely bad and obvious","c":"極其惡劣的","s":"The restaurant's egregious hygiene failures, such as rats in the kitchen, shocked the inspectors, so it was closed down immediately.","t":"這家餐廳極其惡劣的衛生缺失，例如廚房裡有老鼠，讓稽查員大為震驚，所以它被立即勒令停業。"},{"w":"enormity","p":"n.","d":"the great size or seriousness of a problem","c":"嚴重性；巨大","s":"The enormity of world hunger can feel overwhelming, but small actions like donating food still make a difference.","t":"全球飢餓問題的嚴重性可能令人難以承受，但像捐贈食物這樣的小行動仍然能帶來改變。"},{"w":"entitlement","p":"n.","d":"the right to have or receive something","c":"應得的權利","s":"Many people believe that food is a basic entitlement for every child, so free school lunches should be offered everywhere.","t":"許多人認為食物是每個孩子的基本權利，所以應該在各地提供免費的學校午餐。"},{"w":"escalation","p":"n.","d":"a rapid increase in size or seriousness","c":"升級；加劇","s":"The escalation of the trade war raised food prices, and ordinary families felt the effects at the supermarket.","t":"貿易戰的升級推高了食品價格，而一般家庭在超市就能感受到影響。"},{"w":"exclusion","p":"n.","d":"the act of not allowing someone or something to take part","c":"排除；排斥","s":"The exclusion of small farmers from big supermarket contracts is unfair, so some shops are now changing their policy.","t":"將小農排除在大型超市合約之外是不公平的，所以一些商店現在正在改變政策。"},{"w":"feasibility","p":"n.","d":"how possible or practical something is","c":"可行性","s":"The team studied the feasibility of growing coffee in Taiwan, and they found that some mountain areas were ideal.","t":"這個團隊研究了在台灣種咖啡的可行性，而他們發現某些山區非常理想。"},{"w":"flagrant","p":"adj.","d":"shocking and done openly","c":"明目張膽的","s":"Selling dyed vegetables as organic is a flagrant breach of the law, and the shop owner was heavily fined.","t":"把染色蔬菜當作有機產品販售是明目張膽的違法行為，而店主被重罰。"},{"w":"frugality","p":"n.","d":"the habit of not wasting money or food","c":"節儉","s":"My grandparents' frugality taught me not to waste rice, and I still finish every grain in my bowl.","t":"祖父母的節儉教會我不要浪費米飯，而我到現在仍會吃完碗裡的每一粒米。"},{"w":"harbinger","p":"n.","d":"a sign that something is going to happen","c":"預兆；先兆","s":"The first plum flowers are a harbinger of spring, so farmers start preparing their fields when they appear.","t":"第一批梅花是春天的預兆，所以梅花一開，農民就開始整地。"},{"w":"homogenise","p":"v.","d":"to make things the same or similar","c":"使同質化","s":"Global fast-food chains may homogenise eating habits, but local night markets keep traditional dishes alive.","t":"全球速食連鎖店可能會讓飲食習慣同質化，但本地夜市讓傳統小吃得以延續。"},{"w":"immeasurable","p":"adj.","d":"too large to be measured","c":"無法衡量的；無限的","s":"The value of bees to farming is immeasurable, because without them many fruits and nuts would disappear.","t":"蜜蜂對農業的價值是無法衡量的，因為沒有牠們，許多水果和堅果就會消失。"},{"w":"impediment","p":"n.","d":"something that makes progress difficult","c":"障礙；阻礙","s":"High land prices are a major impediment for young farmers, so the government now rents out public land cheaply.","t":"高地價是年輕農民的一大障礙，所以政府現在以低價出租公有土地。"},{"w":"imperil","p":"v.","d":"to put something in danger","c":"危及","s":"Rising sea levels could imperil rice farming in coastal areas, so scientists are testing salt-tolerant varieties.","t":"海平面上升可能危及沿海地區的稻作，所以科學家正在測試耐鹽品種。"},{"w":"imprudent","p":"adj.","d":"not wise or sensible","c":"不智的；輕率的","s":"It would be imprudent to plant all your fields with one crop, because a single disease could destroy everything.","t":"把所有田地都種同一種作物是不明智的，因為單一病害就可能摧毀一切。"},{"w":"inaccessible","p":"adj.","d":"impossible or very difficult to reach","c":"難以到達的；無法取得的","s":"The landslide left the mountain village inaccessible, so helicopters had to drop food for the residents.","t":"山崩讓這座山村無法進出，所以直升機必須為居民空投食物。"},{"w":"inconsistency","p":"n.","d":"the state of not being the same or regular","c":"不一致","s":"Customers complained about the inconsistency of the coffee, because it tasted different every time they ordered it.","t":"顧客抱怨咖啡的品質不一致，因為每次點的味道都不一樣。"},{"w":"indicative","p":"adj.","d":"showing or suggesting something","c":"表明的；暗示的","s":"Yellow leaves are often indicative of a lack of nutrients, so the farmer tested the soil immediately.","t":"黃葉常表示缺乏養分，所以農夫立刻檢測了土壤。"},{"w":"inequitable","p":"adj.","d":"unfair because some people get more than others","c":"不公平的","s":"The inequitable sharing of profits means that coffee farmers earn very little, while cafes make a lot of money.","t":"利潤不公平的分配意味著咖啡農賺得很少，而咖啡館卻賺了很多錢。"}]},{"unit":15,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 8 (inescapable – volatility)","cards":[{"w":"inescapable","p":"adj.","d":"impossible to avoid","c":"不可避免的","s":"The conclusion is inescapable: we must waste less food, or there will not be enough for everyone by 2050.","t":"結論是無可避免的：我們必須減少浪費食物，否則到2050年將不夠每個人吃。"},{"w":"inflationary","p":"adj.","d":"causing prices to rise","c":"通貨膨脹的","s":"The rise in oil prices had an inflationary effect on food, because transport and fertiliser both became more expensive.","t":"油價上漲對食品產生了通膨效應，因為運輸和肥料都變得更貴了。"},{"w":"inordinate","p":"adj.","d":"far more than is reasonable","c":"過度的","s":"Some families spend an inordinate amount of money on food delivery, but they could save a lot by cooking at home.","t":"有些家庭在外送上花了過多的錢，但他們如果在家做飯就能省下很多。"},{"w":"malpractice","p":"n.","d":"careless or illegal behaviour by a professional","c":"不當行為；瀆職","s":"The inspector was accused of malpractice, because he had accepted gifts from the factory he was checking.","t":"這名稽查員被指控瀆職，因為他收受了他正在檢查的工廠所送的禮物。"},{"w":"manifold","p":"adj.","d":"many and of different kinds","c":"多種多樣的","s":"The benefits of school gardens are manifold, because children learn science, exercise and eat more vegetables.","t":"學校菜園的好處多不勝數，因為孩子們能學習科學、運動，並且吃更多蔬菜。"},{"w":"methodology","p":"n.","d":"the methods used in a study or activity","c":"研究方法；方法論","s":"The researchers explained their methodology clearly, so other scientists could repeat the food-waste study in their own cities.","t":"研究人員清楚地說明了他們的研究方法，所以其他科學家能在自己的城市重複這項食物浪費研究。"},{"w":"minuscule","p":"adj.","d":"extremely small","c":"極小的","s":"The amount of pesticide found was minuscule, so experts said the vegetables were still safe to eat.","t":"檢測出的農藥量極少，所以專家說這些蔬菜仍然可以安全食用。"},{"w":"multitude","p":"n.","d":"a very large number of things or people","c":"大量；眾多","s":"The night market offers a multitude of snacks, so first-time visitors often do not know where to begin.","t":"夜市提供眾多小吃，所以第一次來的遊客常常不知道該從哪裡開始。"},{"w":"objectionable","p":"adj.","d":"unpleasant and likely to offend","c":"令人反感的","s":"Neighbours found the smell from the pig farm objectionable, so they complained to the city council.","t":"鄰居們覺得養豬場的氣味令人反感，所以他們向市議會投訴。"},{"w":"omission","p":"n.","d":"something that has been left out","c":"遺漏；省略","s":"The omission of peanuts from the ingredient list was dangerous, because a customer with an allergy became very ill.","t":"成分表中遺漏花生是很危險的，因為一位過敏的顧客因此病得很嚴重。"},{"w":"overreliance","p":"n.","d":"depending too much on something","c":"過度依賴","s":"overreliance on a single crop is risky, so the government encourages farmers to grow several different kinds.","t":"過度依賴單一作物是有風險的，所以政府鼓勵農民種植好幾種不同的作物。"},{"w":"paradoxically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that seems strange because it is the opposite of what you expect","c":"矛盾地；弔詭地","s":"paradoxically, some of the world's hungriest people are farmers, because they sell their best food to pay their debts.","t":"弔詭的是，世界上最飢餓的一些人竟是農民，因為他們賣掉最好的食物來償還債務。"},{"w":"partake","p":"v.","d":"to eat or drink something; to take part","c":"吃喝；參與","s":"Guests are invited to partake in the harvest meal, and everyone eats together at long tables in the field.","t":"賓客受邀參與豐收餐會，而且大家在田裡的長桌一起用餐。"},{"w":"precedence","p":"n.","d":"the right to be considered more important","c":"優先權","s":"Food safety must take precedence over profit, so the company destroyed the whole batch when one test failed.","t":"食品安全必須優先於利潤，所以當一項檢驗不合格時，公司就銷毀了整批產品。"},{"w":"recurrence","p":"n.","d":"the act of happening again","c":"再次發生；復發","s":"To prevent a recurrence of the outbreak, the farm now disinfects every truck that enters.","t":"為了防止疫情再次發生，這座農場現在會對每一輛進入的卡車消毒。"},{"w":"refinement","p":"n.","d":"a small change that improves something","c":"改良；精煉","s":"After years of refinement, the farmer's tea won first prize, and buyers came from Japan to order it.","t":"經過多年的改良，這位農夫的茶贏得了首獎，而買家從日本前來訂購。"},{"w":"rigour","p":"n.","d":"great care and attention to detail","c":"嚴謹","s":"The testing is done with great rigour, so every batch of baby milk is checked several times.","t":"檢驗以極度嚴謹的方式進行，所以每一批嬰兒奶粉都會經過多次檢查。"},{"w":"speculative","p":"adj.","d":"based on guesses rather than facts","c":"推測的；投機的","s":"Claims that insects will replace meat are still speculative, because most people are not ready to eat them.","t":"昆蟲將取代肉類的說法仍是推測，因為大多數人還沒準備好吃牠們。"},{"w":"undeniable","p":"adj.","d":"clearly true and impossible to doubt","c":"不可否認的","s":"The link between sugary drinks and weight gain is undeniable, but many teenagers still drink them every day.","t":"含糖飲料與體重增加之間的關聯是不可否認的，但許多青少年仍然每天喝。"},{"w":"undervalue","p":"v.","d":"to think something is less important than it really is","c":"低估；輕視","s":"Society tends to undervalue the work of farmers, although we depend on them for every meal we eat.","t":"社會往往低估農民的工作，儘管我們吃的每一餐都仰賴他們。"},{"w":"unintended","p":"adj.","d":"not planned or meant","c":"非預期的","s":"The cheap plastic bags had an unintended result, because many of them ended up in rivers and the sea.","t":"便宜的塑膠袋帶來了非預期的後果，因為許多袋子最後流入了河川和海洋。"},{"w":"unregulated","p":"adj.","d":"not controlled by laws or rules","c":"未受管制的","s":"unregulated street stalls may sell unsafe food, so the city now gives licences only to stalls that pass inspections.","t":"未受管制的路邊攤可能販售不安全的食物，所以市政府現在只發執照給通過檢查的攤位。"},{"w":"unwarranted","p":"adj.","d":"not justified or necessary","c":"不必要的；無根據的","s":"Some fears about frozen food are unwarranted, because freezing keeps most vitamins and stops bacteria from growing.","t":"有些對冷凍食品的擔憂是沒有根據的，因為冷凍能保留大部分維他命並阻止細菌生長。"},{"w":"vigilance","p":"n.","d":"careful attention to notice possible danger","c":"警覺；警惕","s":"Farmers must show constant vigilance during flu season, because one sick bird can spread disease to the whole farm.","t":"禽流感季節期間農民必須時時保持警覺，因為一隻生病的鳥就能把疾病傳遍整座農場。"},{"w":"volatility","p":"n.","d":"the quality of changing suddenly and unpredictably","c":"不穩定；波動性","s":"Price volatility makes farming risky, so farmers who sign fixed-price contracts can sleep better at night.","t":"價格波動讓務農充滿風險，所以簽訂固定價格合約的農民晚上能睡得比較安穩。"}]},{"unit":16,"theme":"Fixed Phrases & Collocations 固定片語與搭配詞","cards":[{"w":"from farm to table","p":"phr.","d":"directly from where food is grown to where it is eaten","c":"從產地到餐桌","s":"The restaurant follows the idea of from farm to table, so the vegetables you eat at lunch were picked that morning.","t":"這家餐廳遵循從產地到餐桌的理念，所以你午餐吃到的蔬菜是當天早上才採收的。"},{"w":"put food on the table","p":"v.phr.","d":"to earn enough money to feed your family","c":"養家糊口","s":"My father works two jobs to put food on the table, but he still finds time to help me with homework.","t":"我爸爸做兩份工作來養家糊口，但他仍會抽空幫我寫功課。"},{"w":"bring home the bacon","p":"v.phr.","d":"to earn money to support a family","c":"賺錢養家","s":"In my family, both of my parents bring home the bacon, so we all share the housework at weekends.","t":"在我們家，爸媽兩個人都賺錢養家，所以週末我們全家一起分擔家事。"},{"w":"go to waste","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be thrown away or not used","c":"被浪費","s":"We packed the leftovers in boxes because we did not want the food to go to waste, and we ate it the next day.","t":"我們把剩菜裝進盒子裡，因為不想讓食物被浪費，而且我們隔天就把它吃掉了。"},{"w":"make hay while the sun shines","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make the most of a good chance while it lasts","c":"趁機行事；把握良機","s":"Mango prices are high this week, so the farmers are picking as fast as they can to make hay while the sun shines.","t":"這週芒果價格很高，所以農民們盡可能快速採收，好把握良機。"},{"w":"reap what you sow","p":"v.phr.","d":"to experience the results of your own actions","c":"自食其果；種瓜得瓜","s":"He never studied during the term, so he reap what you sow when he failed the final exam.","t":"他整學期都沒讀書，所以期末考不及格時，他就自食其果了。"},{"w":"the cream of the crop","p":"n.phr.","d":"the best people or things in a group","c":"精英；佼佼者","s":"Only the cream of the crop are chosen for the national cooking team, and they train for hours every day.","t":"只有佼佼者才會被選入國家烹飪隊，而且他們每天都要訓練好幾個小時。"},{"w":"in season","p":"adj.phr.","d":"(of fruit or vegetables) available and at their best now","c":"當季的","s":"Lychees are only in season for a few weeks in summer, so people buy boxes of them and send them to relatives.","t":"荔枝只在夏天的幾個星期是當季的，所以人們會一箱箱地買來寄給親戚。"},{"w":"out of season","p":"adj.phr.","d":"(of fruit or vegetables) not naturally available at this time","c":"非當季的","s":"Strawberries are expensive when they are out of season, because they have to be flown in from other countries.","t":"草莓在非當季時很貴，因為它們必須從其他國家空運進口。"},{"w":"a bad apple","p":"n.phr.","d":"one bad person who has a bad effect on others","c":"害群之馬","s":"Most food sellers at the market are honest, but a bad apple who sold fake honey has hurt everyone's reputation.","t":"市場裡大部分的攤販都很誠實，但一個賣假蜂蜜的害群之馬損害了大家的名聲。"},{"w":"bear fruit","p":"v.phr.","d":"to produce good results","c":"開花結果；產生成果","s":"The farmer's years of hard work finally bear fruit, and his organic rice is now sold in top restaurants.","t":"這位農夫多年的努力終於開花結果，而他的有機米現在在頂級餐廳販售。"},{"w":"cut back on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to reduce the amount of something you use or eat","c":"減少（使用量）","s":"My doctor told me to cut back on salty snacks, so I now eat fruit when I feel hungry after school.","t":"醫生叫我減少吃鹹的零食，所以現在我放學後肚子餓時改吃水果。"},{"w":"eat out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have a meal in a restaurant rather than at home","c":"外食；上館子","s":"Many people in Taipei eat out almost every day because they work long hours, but cooking at home is usually healthier.","t":"許多台北人幾乎每天都外食，因為他們工時很長，但在家做飯通常比較健康。"},{"w":"food for thought","p":"n.phr.","d":"an idea that makes you think seriously","c":"值得深思的事","s":"The film about food waste gave us food for thought, and our class decided to start a leftovers campaign.","t":"那部關於食物浪費的電影給了我們值得深思的事，而我們班決定發起一項剩菜再利用活動。"},{"w":"have a sweet tooth","p":"v.phr.","d":"to like eating sweet food very much","c":"愛吃甜食","s":"My little sister have a sweet tooth, so my mother hides the chocolate on the top shelf.","t":"我妹妹很愛吃甜食，所以我媽媽把巧克力藏在最上層的架子上。"},{"w":"a piece of cake","p":"n.phr.","d":"something very easy to do","c":"小事一樁；易如反掌","s":"Making dumplings looked difficult at first, but after my grandmother showed me, it was a piece of cake.","t":"包水餃一開始看起來很難，但奶奶示範給我看之後，就變得易如反掌了。"},{"w":"cry over spilt milk","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be upset about something that cannot be changed","c":"為無法挽回的事懊悔","s":"The typhoon destroyed half the crop, but there is no point in cry over spilt milk, so the farmers started replanting.","t":"颱風摧毀了一半的作物，但為無法挽回的事懊悔也沒有用，所以農民們開始重新種植。"},{"w":"sell like hot cakes","p":"v.phr.","d":"to sell very quickly and in large numbers","c":"大賣；搶手","s":"The new pineapple cakes sell like hot cakes at the festival, and the bakery ran out before noon.","t":"新推出的鳳梨酥在節慶上大賣，而這家麵包店中午不到就賣光了。"},{"w":"put all one's eggs in one basket","p":"v.phr.","d":"to depend on only one plan or thing","c":"孤注一擲","s":"Farmers who grow only bananas put all one's eggs in one basket, so one disease could ruin them.","t":"只種香蕉的農民等於孤注一擲，所以一種病害就可能讓他們破產。"},{"w":"bread and butter","p":"n.phr.","d":"the main way someone earns money","c":"主要收入來源；生計","s":"Rice is the bread and butter of this village, but young farmers are also trying coffee and tea to earn more.","t":"稻米是這個村莊的主要收入來源，但年輕農民也在嘗試種咖啡和茶來賺更多錢。"}]}];
